scension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039610#post1039610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yyyyyyyeeeeaaaaaaaaaaahhhhhhhhh.<br /> <br /> Supernatural pheromones that suborn consent are pretty rapey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, come on! With that line of thought, everything that affects your subconscious is rape. That's ridiculous. People are attracted for other people for a various of reasons. Exuding animalistic power, health and being excitingly dangerous, thus desirable is not rape. I don't see why &quot;supernatural pheromones&quot; are more rapey than normal ones.<br /> <br /> Mind-fucking the partner with gifts, disciplines, spheres and such is rape. Being sexy, even unnaturally sexy isn't. You just still need to say yes, you just would be more inclined to do so. But it's happening all the time. Some people are sexier than others. Is it fair? No. Is it natural? yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-28-2017, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T15:31:52-08:00","id":1039630,"title":"","content":"It would be like saying that it is rape for an Appearance 5 woman to sleep with an Appearance 3 man because she is 'influencing' his will with her beauty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T15:37:59-08:00","id":1039632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039593#post1039593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> But the point still stands that life was shit until the Order of Reason began an organized campaign to cleanse all the shadowy puppeteers and dismantle the werewolf rape camps.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. It's debatable and depends on how much your chronicle is resembling the real world. Real world wasn't as shitty as we think, although it was certainly shittier than now. We also have different problems, like air pollution, modern wars and, chemicals in food, etc. they didn't have back in the day. It's just not black and white.<br /> <br /> 2. Oh, the heroic Technocracy saved the humanity from the depredations of the supernatural! Hail for them and applause! Too bad they immediately replaced it with heir own shadowy puppeteerness, brainwashing and surveillance, unethical experiments, careless exploitation of nature and people, and so on and so on. They are causing suffering in a much larger scale than any vampire prince or garou warlord or mage enclave.<br /> <br /> 3. As far as I know, the Order of Reason started a few thousand years after the Impergium ended...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T15:49:20-08:00","id":1039636,"title":"","content":"And it is not like the Garou imposed the Imperium on the majority of humanity. As far as I can tell, it was pretty much a European, North African, and Western Asian thing. The Americas, most of Africa, most of Asia, and Australia did not suffer under the Imperium (so only 20% of humanity suffered from the Imperium). <br /> <br /> And the Fera did other thing than pick on humans. They sealed the greatest bane spirits in existence from the world long before the first Mages stopped being just local wise men or wise women and, for tens of thousands of years, they have been trying to keep humans from breaking those seals. One of the primary reasons why Fera dislike Mages is that the majority of Mages throughout history were willing to release countless evils of the world to just gain an iota of power. The Technocrats are just a more organized manifestation of that tendency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T15:50:39-08:00","id":1039637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039630#post1039630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be like saying that it is rape for an Appearance 5 woman to sleep with an Appearance 3 man because she is 'influencing' his will with her beauty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> Being sexy is not rape, being sexy partly because your supernatural nature isn't rape either.<br /> <br /> Consent is not about being completely unaffected by everything and making a decision without any kind of influence, in some kind of mythically pure, rational state of mind. Consent is about being able to make the decision and not being forced on.<br /> <br /> That Garou are sexy in most people's eyes doesn't force them to sleep with them. They could say &quot;yes, I'm very attracted, but she/hes's still a dick&quot;. However we shouldn't pretend that we aren't affected by subconscious things all the time. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T15:56:09-08:00","id":1039641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039632#post1039632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. It's debatable and depends on how much your chronicle is resembling the real world. Real world wasn't as shitty as we think, although it was certainly shittier than now. We also have different problems, like air pollution, modern wars and, chemicals in food, etc. they didn't have back in the day. It's just not black and white.<br /> <br /> 2. Oh, the heroic Technocracy saved the humanity from the depredations of the supernatural! Hail for them and applause! Too bad they immediately replaced it with heir own shadowy puppeteerness, brainwashing and surveillance, unethical experiments, careless exploitation of nature and people, and so on and so on. They are causing suffering in a much larger scale than any vampire prince or garou warlord or mage enclave.<br /> <br /> 3. As far as I know, the Order of Reason started a few thousand years after the Impergium ended...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The vampires have their masqared now dont they? Garou no longer are able to do rampant slaghter when they get pissed correct? And you don't have selfish Mages throwing fireballs at peasants for giving them a funny look correct?<br /> <br /> But I can tell what we DO have: television, that's a great things against the nighfolk; investigative polices, that's also a great tool against the hidden predators; about all the suffering they're causing: mass education (back in the day you could hope to be an illiterate peasant like your father, your grandfather, and do on, and that your children would have the same fate), mass production of food, households, etc. Back in the day, a tough winter meant the death of your whole village. You have access to all the knowledge of the greatest universities in the world with a simple magik device, like a cel phone. And you no longer are subjected to some local pharaoh that decides to subtract your head on a whim.<br /> <br /> About &quot;rape camps&quot;, humans are not raped by the Garou. They are just sex toys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:01:18-08:00","id":1039645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039637#post1039637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consent is not about being completely unaffected by everything and making a decision without any kind of influence, in some kind of mythically pure, rational state of mind. Consent is about being able to make the decision and not being forced on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Careful here. This argument could be used to justify rape of drunk people, or rape of drugged people.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure this is the kind of thing you intend to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:01:51-08:00","id":1039647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039632#post1039632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. It's debatable and depends on how much your chronicle is resembling the real world. Real world wasn't as shitty as we think, although it was certainly shittier than now. We also have different problems, like air pollution, modern wars and, chemicals in food, etc. they didn't have back in the day. It's just not black and white.</div> </div> </div> </div>Real world also had no culling of humanity by werewolves, no vampiric elder gods and no war between angels and rebelling angels. WoD's history is crazy and is about as historic as Earthdawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:02:53-08:00","id":1039648,"title":"","content":"The way you're describing this animal magnetism really makes it sound like that if a werewolf wants to have sex with a human woman, his animalistic nature is going to flip a switch in her brain, and she's going to have sex with him regardless of whatever she thought was going to happen before that switch was flipped. If a werewolf willfully besots a reluctant partner into sex, and if the human being is incapable of refusal, then that's rape. I don't know the specifics of this power (and really, this is SO squicky that I just wish it had never been featured as a detail in the first place) but you were the one that brought it up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039636#post1039636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it is not like the Garou imposed the Imperium on the majority of humanity. As far as I can tell, it was pretty much a European, North African, and Western Asian thing. The Americas, most of Africa, most of Asia, and Australia did not suffer under the Imperium (so only 20% of humanity suffered from the Imperium).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just going to point out that since the Impergium was in prehistory, MOST OF HUMANITY lived in North Africa, Europe, and Central/Western Asia. <br /> <br /> And by the way, I'm just going to point out that you used the qualifier 'only' to describe the systematic and sustained culling of humanity by our werewolf overlords. Out of curiosity, how large a percentage of humanity has to be subjected to werewolf culling before it's a shitty move?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:18:31-08:00","id":1039659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039641#post1039641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The vampires have their masqared now dont they? Garou no longer are able to do rampant slaghter when they get pissed correct? And you don't have selfish Mages throwing fireballs at peasants for giving them a funny look correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of them were hiding through most of human history, not just since the OoR. You're picturing those as they were normal everyday things. In my book they were more like terrorist actions nowadays. It might be better or worse regionally too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I can tell what we DO have: television, that's a great things against the nighfolk; investigative polices, that's also a great tool against the hidden predators; about all the suffering they're causing: mass education (back in the day you could hope to be an illiterate peasant like your father, your grandfather, and do on, and that your children would have the same fate), mass production of food, households, etc. Back in the day, a tough winter meant the death of your whole village. You have access to all the knowledge of the greatest universities in the world with a simple magik device, like a cel phone. And you no longer are subjected to some local pharaoh that decides to subtract your head on a whim. </div> </div> </div>Oh, the old, &quot;everything good in human history is due to the Technocracy&quot; argument. Yeah, thanks, but no thanks. Humanity did incredible things way before the Union. There were culture, science and the world wasn't as bad as we like to think. The Union played a role in the forming of the modern world, but it's not solely their making. For Voldemort's sake, we have internet because of a Virtual Adept, due to Mage canon!<br /> <br /> It's just not like before the Technocracy: shi-shit-shit and after the Technocracy:everything is bright and shiny. It's just propaganda.<br /> <br /> And don't pretend we don't have a myriad of problems because of things that could be credited as much to the Technocracy's work as the good things. Yeah, we might not froze during winter (yet...), but we have global warming that affects people on a much larger scale than a bad winter. We have the largest extinction of species happening since the dinosaurs. Millions of people are on the road and suffering wars because the differences in world incomes and said global warming. The list goes on. Those things might be even worse in the WoD, but frankly, they doesn1t have to, it's pretty bad as reality. We are just living in a bubble in the Western world but that won't last indefinitely. <br /> <br /> So, I don't argue that the OoR didn't have valid points and good intentions. I acknowledge that the Union did good things for humanity. However, at large it embodies everything that could go wrong with us if being unchecked and driven by fear and greed and self-righteousness.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:25:26-08:00","id":1039664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039645#post1039645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Careful here. This argument could be used to justify rape of drunk people, or rape of drugged people.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure this is the kind of thing you intend to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I didn't intend that and I don't think that it could be justify that. Drunk, especially badly drunk and drugged people are not in the state to be able to make clear decisions. They are especially vulnerable. That's absolutely not the same as seeing someone as sexy while you're more-or-less sober and saying yes without the other party doing any kind of forcing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:28:24-08:00","id":1039666,"title":"","content":"Have either of you guys maybe considered that...<br /> ... I don't know.... that you're both right about this?<br /> <br /> Why does have to be a case of &quot;technocracy made everything better&quot; vs &quot;everything was better before thetechnocracy&quot;?<br /> <br /> Why not just &quot;technocracy made things different&quot;<br /> Some things are an improvement, after all, without a codified consensus, computers and telephones never would have been available, so the masses wouldn't be able to have remote discussions without a hell of a lot of work and study.<br /> <br /> But at the same time the unified consensus relies heavily upon their everyone believing it as much as they believe that up is above them. That requires a lot of control, a great deal of herding, and a steady stream of new tech coming out in order to avoid stagnation, and the resulting uproar of discontent.<br /> <br /> The technocracy have, for better and worse, changed the world.<br /> <br /> Whether you prefer their reality or not is more a question of taste than morals.<br /> <br /> This is WoD. There are no preferable choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:30:14-08:00","id":1039668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039541#post1039541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, even in a crossover with MtA. The idea that Fera (or Changelings) can access more areas of Reality than Mages does not negate anything about the nature of Mages, as it is the Awakened Avatar of Mages that gives then their power (and the Paradigm accepted by the Awakened Avatar of Mages that shapes their perceptions of Reality). It is just an acknowledgement of the limitations of individual Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I went and asked one of the people I know who actually KNOWS werewolf stuff. Werewolves deal with Subspace. Also known as Etherspace in MtA. It looks like Conventional space AKA 'real' outer space but it's not.<br /> <br /> They don't do anything in conventional space. Which is actual real space. Also litterally every human on the planet has an avatar. That's what the Consensus is.<br /> <br /> So no. Fera can't access 'more layers' of reality than the technocrats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039553#post1039553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just one thing:<br /> If the Technos are the much needed guardians of humankind, who exactly did their job before they were around?<br /> Could it not be, that the Union created (unconsciously) the things and problems they fight (diseases, things from beyond, RDs, etc.)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you ever played a game called space station 13? If not, I'll give you a quick run down. There's a space station and you and 60+ other people perform roles on the station. 1-3 of those people are actually traitors. Out to destroy things.<br /> <br /> Now, while not making any modifications to the station leaves you somewhat vulnerable. It's also inconspicuous. The moment you build yourself a fortress in one of the departments EVERYONE will be trying to take a go at it.<br /> <br /> Same principle. Before they COULD but didn't really see the point. So you didn't get more than one or two a century. Then the Technocrats said &quot;Fuck this shit.&quot; and fortified earth against intrusion.<br /> <br /> You can bet THAT got the unknown horrors attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:31:23-08:00","id":1039669,"title":"","content":"He wasn't a Virtual Adept at the time, he were still a technocrat; the VAs only became what they are now after Alan Turing had gone away.<br /> <br /> About the poor, the hungry, the wars yadda yadda yadda, all those things are still a thing, and yet they were far WORSE just a century ago. The industrial revolution brought an exponential raise on the global wealth; a middle class person today have a better life than any medieval King. The poverty we still have is a legacy from the historical misery throughout the entire human era, it's NOT a byproduct from the modern world. And about wars, we actually have less of them, globally, than ever before (you can thank the atomic power for that).<br /> About the environment... Yeah, that's really a problem. However, you're not willing to exchange your house for a wooden hut to help fix it, are you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:31:58-08:00","id":1039670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039648#post1039648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way you're describing this animal magnetism really makes it sound like that if a werewolf wants to have sex with a human woman, his animalistic nature is going to flip a switch in her brain, and she's going to have sex with him regardless of whatever she thought was going to happen before that switch was flipped. If a werewolf willfully besots a reluctant partner into sex, and if the human being is incapable of refusal, then that's rape. I don't know the specifics of this power (and really, this is SO squicky that I just wish it had never been featured as a detail in the first place) but you were the one that brought it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I took it as you just would find them more attractive for the same reason that a lot of people find &quot;bad boys&quot; attractive. It's not like flipping a switch and taking away the capability of making decisions, but more like feeling aspects that might attract you even more intensely from them and thus making them more attractive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:54:00-08:00","id":1039684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039668#post1039668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, I went and asked one of the people I know who actually KNOWS werewolf stuff. Werewolves deal with Subspace. Also known as Etherspace in MtA. It looks like Conventional space AKA 'real' outer space but it's not.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have been playing WtA since 1993 and MtA since 1995, so I would ask you to apologize concerning your assumptions about who knows what about which games. You can disagree with me, that is fine, but it another thing to disrespect my gaming credentials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:56:58-08:00","id":1039685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039630#post1039630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be like saying that it is rape for an Appearance 5 woman to sleep with an Appearance 3 man because she is 'influencing' his will with her beauty.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that isn't an invalid position.<br /> <br /> Also I meant that *I* don't know werewolf. So I went to someone who did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T17:06:18-08:00","id":1039690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039666#post1039666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does have to be a case of &quot;technocracy made everything better&quot; vs &quot;everything was better before thetechnocracy&quot;?<br /> <br /> Why not just &quot;technocracy made things different&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's play a little game.<br /> <br /> A trickster god pulls you out of time and space, and says to you that you're going to be reborn. The trickster god is randomly going to assign you to be born at some point in the world prior to the year 2017. The one thing you get to choose is the year you're born into.<br /> <br /> You do not get to choose your genetic makeup. The social class of your parents. Their ethnicity. Their nationality. Their wealth. The number of other siblings that exist in the household, or your birth order relative to any of your hypothetical siblings. You do not get to choose your gender, your sexual orientation (unless you believe it's a matter of choice. Then choose away). You do not retain any knowledge you have acquired during this lifetime. This is a pure rebirth with only the year up to you, which, the trickster god points out, wasn't even an option to you the first time around. Every other detail about your life is the result of pure chance<br /> <br /> Now. Given that game, what year do you choose, and why? And if the answer is anything other than &quot;the last ten or twenty years,&quot; then I think we've answered your question about why the proposition &quot;the technocracy has made things progressively better for everyone&quot; is a more defensible position than some kind of happy medium seeking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":1515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","user":"BenjCano","date":". 01-28-2017, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T17:13:08-08:00","id":1039695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039690#post1039690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's play a little game.<br /> <br /> A trickster god pulls you out of time and space, and says to you that you're going to be reborn. The trickster god is randomly going to assign you to be born at some point in the world. The one thing you get to choose is the year you're born into. <br /> <br /> You do not get to choose your genetic makeup. The social class of your parents. Their ethnicity. Their nationality. Their wealth. The number of other siblings that exist in the household, or your birth order relative to any of your hypothetical siblings. You do not get to choose your gender, your sexual orientation (unless you believe it's a matter of choice. Then choose away). You do not retain any knowledge you have acquired during this lifetime. This is a pure rebirth with only the year up to you, which, the trickster god points out, wasn't even an option to you the first time around. Every other detail about your life is the result of pure chance<br /> <br /> Now. Given that game, what year do you choose, and why? And if the answer is anything other than &quot;the last ten or twenty years,&quot; then I think we've answered your question about why the proposition &quot;the technocracy has made things progressively better for everyone&quot; is a more defensible position than some kind of happy medium seeking.</div> </div> </div> </div>First question. Which time period am I being pulled from? Because my answer will depend on what I am accustomed to.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you would assume that I should chose the option of going far into the future since things will always be better there.<br /> <br /> Also, if I couldn't chose any of these demographics, I would think it made little difference. If I chose the Victorian era, I'd have the same chance of being among the wealthy elite as I do being a slave and everywhere in between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-28-2017, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T17:17:23-08:00","id":1039698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039666#post1039666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have either of you guys maybe considered that...<br /> ... I don't know.... that you're both right about this?<br /> <br /> Why does have to be a case of &quot;technocracy made everything better&quot; vs &quot;everything was better before thetechnocracy&quot;?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you look closer, it's usually the pro-technocrats who are on the extreme end of the argument and usually it's also them claiming that according to the pro-traditions people, everything was better back in the day. So, making a black and white statement and then strawmaning the other side. Pro-Traditions people usually explicitly say that the Traditions wouldn't want to cast away the trappings of the modern world and go back to neolithic.<br /> <br /> I guess, the Union, as written needs more justification to be sympathetic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why not just &quot;technocracy made things different&quot;<br /> Some things are an improvement, after all, without a codified consensus, computers and telephones never would have been available, so the masses wouldn't be able to have remote discussions without a hell of a lot of work and study. </div> </div> </div>I'm not even sure that elecronics are working because of the consensus. Humanity had pretty sophisticated technologies before the OoR. It might be more prone to malfunctions, but I don't think it would be gone with the consensus shifting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039669#post1039669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He wasn't a Virtual Adept at the time, he were still a technocrat; the VAs only became what they are now after Alan Turing had gone away.</div> </div> </div> </div>They debated leaving before that and eventually left because how the Union treated Turing. So, his vision is hardly a Technocratic thing, they wanted to smother it. Then the VAs had it enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About the poor, the hungry, the wars yadda yadda yadda, all those things are still a thing, and yet they were far WORSE just a century ago. The industrial revolution brought an exponential raise on the global wealth; a middle class person today have a better life than any medieval King. The poverty we still have is a legacy from the historical misery throughout the entire human era, it's NOT a byproduct from the modern world. </div> </div> </div>Comparing medieval kings with today's middle class is just unfair.<br /> <br /> If anything, the disparity between the rich and poor grown even further in the majority of the world. A medieval noble didn't lived as much differently from a middle-class citizen or even from a peasant than a member of the upper class living nowadays in comparison to the working-class. Also, a lot of people out there living a life pretty much like the ones a century before. Also, in the WoD, the Union more-or-less ruled during the earlier centuries. They're ruling <i>exactly </i>because of centuries of exploitation of other people and the world.<br /> <br /> The industrial revolution also brought tons of misery with them. Read up on the topic how much a medieval villager worked in comparison to someone during the revolution and even today. The industrialism brought workhouses, coal-smog and other ugliness too. I'm rather living today than in earlier times, but I'd rather live in the medieval times, or renaissance than during the industrial revolution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And about wars, we actually have less of them, globally, than ever before (you can thank the atomic power for that). </div> </div> </div>And much more people are affected by them than in earlier times. Go to the Middle-East, Africa, or South America and say THEM that we have a safer world and less wars now than then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About the environment... Yeah, that's really a problem. However, you're not willing to exchange your house for a wooden hut to help fix it, are you? </div> </div> </div>I'm asking the last time: why is that like that every time in the eyes of the pro-Technocrats? Or, IRL in the eyes of anti-green people? Why you just assume that it's either or? Why we couldn't have a middle ground, but just the two extremes? Can't we really have progress and improvement without utter exploitation of resources, of the planet and environment and the people?<br /> <br /> Oh, and for the record, I'm Hungarian and living in a suburban area. We're saving as much energy as we could, because we are lower middle class. We have an older car, but using it just as much as we have to and using public transportation most of the time. I don't have a laptop, I don't have a smartphone. It's not whining, we aren't poor either, at least not as I see &quot;poor&quot;, but we're far-far behind the living standards of an average USA or Western European citizen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T17:25:16-08:00","id":1039701,"title":"","content":"And it really would not matter even if we were deposited into 2017. If we end up in the developing world, where 80% of humanity lives, our life will suck (yes, it may suck differently than it sucked for our ancestors, but it will still suck). The majority of us live in the developed world, so we benefit from the world created by the oppression of the working classes of the developing world (which is the world created by the Technocracy in cWoD). If we live within the developed world, we benefit from the environmental and labor abuses suffered by the inhabitants of the developing world so we can purchase jeans for $20 a pair or palm oil for $10 a liter. I actually like the world cWoD better than our world because at least there is someone to blame for the abuses other than just the greed of the few and the acquiescence of the many.in the developed world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 01-28-2017, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T17:26:50-08:00","id":1039703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039666#post1039666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have either of you guys maybe considered that...<br /> ... I don't know.... that you're both right about this?<br /> <br /> Why does have to be a case of &quot;technocracy made everything better&quot; vs &quot;everything was better before thetechnocracy&quot;?<br /> <br /> Why not just &quot;technocracy made things different&quot;<br /> Some things are an improvement, after all, without a codified consensus, computers and telephones never would have been available, so the masses wouldn't be able to have remote discussions without a hell of a lot of work and study.<br /> <br /> But at the same time the unified consensus relies heavily upon their everyone believing it as much as they believe that up is above them. That requires a lot of control, a great deal of herding, and a steady stream of new tech coming out in order to avoid stagnation, and the resulting uproar of discontent.<br /> <br /> The technocracy have, for better and worse, changed the world.<br /> <br /> Whether you prefer their reality or not is more a question of taste than morals.<br /> <br /> This is WoD. There are no preferable choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok other people quoted this so I am going to do the same, and expand on it just a bit.<br /> <br /> Now if you want to do run a Tradition game you need to highlight the positive things, and minimize the bad things Freedom of choice is a big one, as is the idea reality should be full of possibilities is another. Since the Technocracy makes such wonderful bad guys we can't ignore that so we need to take advantage of their idea of static reality. <br /> <br /> But if you run a Technocracy based game the idea switch. Many of the good things about the Technocracy have been brought up so no need to rehash them. For bad guys you can still use part of the Union and work with the idea of Big Brother is always watching. There is also how the Traditions only care about them selves, and not the masses. But the best bad for a Technocracy game in my opinion are Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T17:31:19-08:00","id":1039705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039690#post1039690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's play a little game.<br /> <br /> A trickster god pulls you out of time and space, and says to you that you're going to be reborn. The trickster god is randomly going to assign you to be born at some point in the world prior to the year 2017. The one thing you get to choose is the year you're born into.<br /> <br /> You do not get to choose your genetic makeup. The social class of your parents. Their ethnicity. Their nationality. Their wealth. The number of other siblings that exist in the household, or your birth order relative to any of your hypothetical siblings. You do not get to choose your gender, your sexual orientation (unless you believe it's a matter of choice. Then choose away). You do not retain any knowledge you have acquired during this lifetime. This is a pure rebirth with only the year up to you, which, the trickster god points out, wasn't even an option to you the first time around. Every other detail about your life is the result of pure chance<br /> <br /> Now. Given that game, what year do you choose, and why? And if the answer is anything other than &quot;the last ten or twenty years,&quot; then I think we've answered your question about why the proposition &quot;the technocracy has made things progressively better for everyone&quot; is a more defensible position than some kind of happy medium seeking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have two problems with this:<br /> <br /> 1. It entirely depends on the where and which social strata? I'd rather be a citizen in the Italian city states during the 1400's than an average person in some kind of 3rd World hellhole now.<br /> <br /> 2. It's (again) assuming that everything better today is due to the Technocracy, like there wasn't any kind of development, progression or science before them. Like humanity wouldn't be capable of progress without the monolithic power of the Union. The problem is that according to the game, it's just untrue.<br /> <br /> The technological and social progress never was the problem with the Union and most members of the Traditions never wanted to go back before electricity. The problem is that too much eggs got broken during the making of the omelet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-28-2017, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T17:46:33-08:00","id":1039715,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Traditions are not a bunch of anti-technology Luddites, they just want to not be ruled by a criminal conspiracy of genocidal fascist maniacs. Without the Union, technological and scientific progress may have been accelerated, as the benefits of technology and science would have been spread more evenly across the Earth, and the average nominal per capita income would have been $25,000 per person (for 3 billion people) rather than the $10,000 per person (for 7.5 billion people). With the acceleration of technological and scientific progress, Lunar mining colonies would have been established by the end of the 1970s, Mars colonies would have been established by the end of the 1980s, Orbital Satellite Arrays capable of providing limitless energy would have been finished by the end of the 1990s, Asteroid colonies would have been established by the end of the 2000s, and we would be discussing the establishment of Titan colonies to harvest nitrogen for the space colonies by the end of the 2010s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"ke