he-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T18:48:55-08:00","id":1039735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039715#post1039715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Traditions are not a bunch of anti-technology Luddites, they just want to not be ruled by a criminal conspiracy of genocidal fascist maniacs. Without the Union, technological and scientific progress may have been accelerated, as the benefits of technology and science would have been spread more evenly across the Earth, and the average nominal per capita income would have been $25,000 per person (for 3 billion people) rather than the $10,000 per person (for 7.5 billion people). With the acceleration of technological and scientific progress, Lunar mining colonies would have been established by the end of the 1970s, Mars colonies would have been established by the end of the 1980s, Orbital Satellite Arrays capable of providing limitless energy would have been finished by the end of the 1990s, Asteroid colonies would have been established by the end of the 2000s, and we would be discussing the establishment of Titan colonies to harvest nitrogen for the space colonies by the end of the 2010s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without the Union. Science and Technology would not exist at <i>all.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T19:14:46-08:00","id":1039746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039735#post1039735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without the Union. Science and Technology would not exist at <i>all.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That's nonsense. Sorry, it is. Science and technology, or even arts and philosophy didn't came out of nowhere with the OoR. The people weren't idiots before them. They built amazing things, knew a lot about mathematics, nature and medicine and had very sophisticated technologies, according to those eras. They are a lot of misconceptions about how much they did know. Yes, we know a lot more things, and they had a lot of false beliefs and such too, but our sciences were built upon their knowledge. <br /> <br /> Accidentally, it's a very renaissance-y and Victorian way of thinking that people of earlier ages were ignorant, filthy buggers, which way of thinking is accidentally completely ignorant of how things were and built upon self-justification, the notion of cultural superiority and working on wrong data and/or accentuating only the worst extremities. <br /> <br /> Guess whose two eras were when the Technocracy established it's workings, beliefs and system in the setting?<br /> <br /> I say that as someone who loves both cultural era, as they are very interesting ones, but it's true nevertheless. They were just soooo full of themselves based upon false misconceptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T19:23:16-08:00","id":1039749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039698#post1039698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you look closer, it's usually the pro-technocrats who are on the extreme end of the argument and usually it's also them claiming that according to the pro-traditions people, everything was better back in the day. So, making a black and white statement and then strawmaning the other side. Pro-Traditions people usually explicitly say that the Traditions wouldn't want to cast away the trappings of the modern world and go back to neolithic.<br /> <br /> I guess, the Union, as written needs more justification to be sympathetic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not even sure that elecronics are working because of the consensus. Humanity had pretty sophisticated technologies before the OoR. It might be more prone to malfunctions, but I don't think it would be gone with the consensus shifting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They debated leaving before that and eventually left because how the Union treated Turing. So, his vision is hardly a Technocratic thing, they wanted to smother it. Then the VAs had it enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Comparing medieval kings with today's middle class is just unfair.<br /> <br /> If anything, the disparity between the rich and poor grown even further in the majority of the world. A medieval noble didn't lived as much differently from a middle-class citizen or even from a peasant than a member of the upper class living nowadays in comparison to the working-class. Also, a lot of people out there living a life pretty much like the ones a century before. Also, in the WoD, the Union more-or-less ruled during the earlier centuries. They're ruling <i>exactly </i>because of centuries of exploitation of other people and the world.<br /> <br /> The industrial revolution also brought tons of misery with them. Read up on the topic how much a medieval villager worked in comparison to someone during the revolution and even today. The industrialism brought workhouses, coal-smog and other ugliness too. I'm rather living today than in earlier times, but I'd rather live in the medieval times, or renaissance than during the industrial revolution.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And much more people are affected by them than in earlier times. Go to the Middle-East, Africa, or South America and say THEM that we have a safer world and less wars now than then.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm asking the last time: why is that like that every time in the eyes of the pro-Technocrats? Or, IRL in the eyes of anti-green people? Why you just assume that it's either or? Why we couldn't have a middle ground, but just the two extremes? Can't we really have progress and improvement without utter exploitation of resources, of the planet and environment and the people?<br /> <br /> Oh, and for the record, I'm Hungarian and living in a suburban area. We're saving as much energy as we could, because we are lower middle class. We have an older car, but using it just as much as we have to and using public transportation most of the time. I don't have a laptop, I don't have a smartphone. It's not whining, we aren't poor either, at least not as I see &amp;quot;poor&amp;quot;, but we're far-far behind the living standards of an average USA or Western European citizen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, spare me the lecturing about &quot;oh, the poor third world&quot;. Im a Brazilian, and I have lived in Brazil my entire life. I know EXACTLY what it is in South America... It just happens it's were I was born and were I live. My family came from the slums. And when I say slums, I don't mean Brooklin. It means those places like in Africa or India were people live above sewer-rivers in wodden houses. That type of slum. I know the ugliness of the world in first hand. And I tell you, it got better, and it gets better every year. <br /> <br /> In here, it only got WORSE in the last decade as a courtesy for all the &quot;equalitarian&quot; fighters, the socialists from the workers party that gave Brazil the worse crises in history and stole ONE TRILLION DOLLARS from the goverment.<br /> <br /> So, in here, it's not the evil white european that keeps my fellow countrymen deep in the shit. Its the guys that talk about &quot;equality&quot; that makes my country a ruin.<br /> <br /> The problem of enviroment, is about hypocrisy. The pro Green love to talk bad about industrialization, like it were a big Satan in the world. But wouldn't go back to the woods in order to &quot;save the planet&quot;.<br /> So, of course a middle ground would help. But don't say it like industries are terrible things. It's those industries that make your food, so you don't have to starve to death trying to hunt rats in caves. It's those industries that make your clothes so you don't freeze to death. And it's those industries that made your home so that you don't need to stay in the open on the wilds, at risk of being killed by wolves during the night. So, you may ask for <i>less</i>, indeed we don't need all that much (I'm also not a rich person and I don't waste money like water on frivolities), but don't say that industrialization were a bad thing for the human kind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T19:32:08-08:00","id":1039751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039701#post1039701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it really would not matter even if we were deposited into 2017. If we end up in the developing world, where 80% of humanity lives, our life will suck (yes, it may suck differently than it sucked for our ancestors, but it will still suck). The majority of us live in the developed world, so we benefit from the world created by the oppression of the working classes of the developing world (which is the world created by the Technocracy in cWoD). If we live within the developed world, we benefit from the environmental and labor abuses suffered by the inhabitants of the developing world so we can purchase jeans for $20 a pair or palm oil for $10 a liter. I actually like the world cWoD better than our world because at least there is someone to blame for the abuses other than just the greed of the few and the acquiescence of the many.in the developed world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh please. I live in Brazil. 70.000 murders every year, a lot more than in Syria AT WAR. Spare me. I KNOW how it is; and I tell you, Brazil, or Africa, or Middle East, or India, or whatever third world country, are not crap places because of the &quot;evil white men&quot;. They are crap places because they have crap goverments. THAT'S IT.<br /> <br /> I tell you because I live it, everyday: my beloved Brazil, for example, is a sewer (it really is, most of you have no idea). But there is no American, or German or Japonese that comes here to exploit us. My country is a shithole because, well, amongst other things, they just stole 1.000.000.000.000 of dollars from the people over the last decade. That's why my country is a crap, despite being the 5th biggest country in the world, the 5th population, and many mineral resources and agricultural potential.<br /> <br /> It's not the americans that keep my country poor; it's my own countrymen that do it.<br /> <br /> The same holds true for any other African, Asian or Latin American country","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T19:41:16-08:00","id":1039757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039749#post1039749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem of enviroment, is about hypocrisy. The pro Green love to talk bad about industrialization, like it were a big Satan in the world. But wouldn't go back to the woods in order to &quot;save the planet&quot;.<br /> So, of course a middle ground would help. But don't say it like industries are terrible things. It's those industries that make your food, so you don't have to starve to death trying to hunt rats in caves. It's those industries that make your clothes so you don't freeze to death. And it's those industries that made your home so that you don't need to stay in the open on the wilds, at risk of being killed by wolves during the night. So, you may ask for <i>less</i>, indeed we don't need all that much (I'm also not a rich person and I don't waste money like water on frivolities), but don't say that industrialization were a bad thing for the human kind</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you're speaking in gross extremities. If, in your mind it's only full-blown industrialism or going back to the woods, then I think further argument is moot and I'm done with it. I'm aware how it's hypocrisy to say to a person from the 3rd world, that we shouldn't burn as much coal and oil, that they shouldn't cut down all the forests and hunt down endangered animals. I know they'd want to send me to hell for saying things like that. Still, those things are true and the fact that those things are happening, in a large part, because how many people are eating up how much percentage of the world's income makes it even worse, because we could do MUCH better with the resources.<br /> <br /> That industrialism makes life easier doesn't mean there aren't a million problems with it and that we shouldn't strive for better. Besides, nobody said that industrialism is the devil, just that it has considerable drawbacks too and that there is a point, where you can't justify everything in the name of progress and living better, especially when that &quot;living better&quot; has serious dangers regarding the future.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T19:46:55-08:00","id":1039762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039746#post1039746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's nonsense. Sorry, it is. Science and technology, or even arts and philosophy didn't came out of nowhere with the OoR. The people weren't idiots before them. They built amazing things, knew a lot about mathematics, nature and medicine and had very sophisticated technologies, according to those eras. They are a lot of misconceptions about how much they did know. Yes, we know a lot more things, and they had a lot of false beliefs and such too, but our sciences were built upon their knowledge. <br /> <br /> Accidentally, it's a very renaissance-y and Victorian way of thinking that people of earlier ages were ignorant, filthy buggers, which way of thinking is accidentally completely ignorant of how things were and built upon self-justification, the notion of cultural superiority and working on wrong data and/or accentuating only the worst extremities. <br /> <br /> Guess whose two eras were when the Technocracy established it's workings, beliefs and system in the setting?<br /> <br /> I say that as someone who loves both cultural era, as they are very interesting ones, but it's true nevertheless. They were just soooo full of themselves based upon false misconceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, what you're saying is the nonsense. Before the Order of Reason, people new their shit. Ok, that's not wrong. But it wasn't science. And it wasn't technology. Not in the WoD. The civilizations would use the maths of the proto hermetics, like the ethruscs from Rome.<br /> <br /> But there was no science.<br /> <br /> Science, in the WoD, is a result of the technocratic CONSENSUS.<br /> <br /> Before the Technocrats, diseases TRULY were caused by evil spirits.There WEREN'T microscopic pathogens back there; and there was no REAL technology. Because crystals could be used to generate light for example, without el\u00e9ctrica power. And a piece of stick could throw fireballs.<br /> <br /> In the WoD, the Order of Reason CREATED the scientific &quot;facts&quot;, it did not DISCOVERED them.<br /> <br /> So, &quot;science and technology&quot; truly are inventions of the Order of Reason and the Union.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T19:55:18-08:00","id":1039768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039751#post1039751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh please. I live in Brazil. 70.000 murders every year, a lot more than in Syria AT WAR. Spare me. I KNOW how it is; and I tell you, Brazil, or Africa, or Middle East, or India, or whatever third world country, are not crap places because of the &quot;evil white men&quot;. They are crap places because they have crap goverments. THAT'S IT.<br /> <br /> I tell you because I live it, everyday: my beloved Brazil, for example, is a sewer (it really is, most of you have no idea). But there is no American, or German or Japonese that comes here to exploit us. My country is a shithole because, well, amongst other things, they just stole 1.000.000.000.000 of dollars from the people over the last decade. That's why my country is a crap, despite being the 5th biggest country in the world, the 5th population, and many mineral resources and agricultural potential.<br /> <br /> It's not the americans that keep my country poor; it's my own countrymen that do it.<br /> <br /> The same holds true for any other African, Asian or Latin American country</div> </div> </div> </div>And you don't take into consideration any historical reasons and bigger world economics.<br /> <br /> Local politics aren't existing in a bubble. For example in here, Hungary, we're in the situation we are, because of shitty governments, just like your country. But those governments aren't independent from other countries' and from corporations. It doesn't mean that they're innocent victims of evil overlords abroad, it's just hat economy and politics are complex webs and nobody is on her own, be it good or bad.<br /> <br /> We got tremendous money from the EU, for example, while Western corporations bought up and then broken down the majority of the local industry to make Eastern Europe a market. Those things are just not black and white.<br /> <br /> Also, things didn't came out of nowhere, there is a historical reason of why the things the way they are and a large part of it is indeed Western exploitation. HOWEVER, saying that everything is the fault of the eeeviiiiil Western White Male is also a gross exaggeration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T19:56:28-08:00","id":1039769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's nonsense. Sorry, it is. Science and technology, or even arts and philosophy didn't came out of nowhere with the OoR.</div> </div> </div> </div>This it's something that I have repeated over, and over, and over, and over...<br /> <br /> There's always people that think that science was invented by the Technocracy because that's the propaganda Technocrats sell in their books. And for some reason people buys this, even when it's explicitly stated to be IOC propaganda. Like if Pythagoras would think itself as a Technocrat, if he was raised from the dead. Or like 2 of the Conventions of the Technocracy hadnt come from the Order of Hermes.<br /> <br /> No, science wasn't invented nor created by the Union. They just control it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-28-2017, 11:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T19:56:41-08:00","id":1039770,"title":"","content":"And where do you think that $1 trillion went? It went to American and European banks, invested in American and European companies, buying American and European properties, and vacationing in American and European cities. It is the same thing with oligarchs all over the world, we welcome their money as long as they keep their people poor and grateful for the scraps that we leave them.<br /> <br /> America and Russia pretty much ruled the world from 1945-1991 and, since 1991, America pretty much ruled the playground by itself. Yes, China grew wealthy...off of providing America and Europe with cheap goods. Yes, India is getting wealthier...off of providing America and Europe with cheap services. It is not like they have much of a choice really though, as America has a nasty habit of assassinating leaders that will not play ball and of invading countries of leaders they cannot assassinate. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:03:18-08:00","id":1039771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039757#post1039757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, you're speaking in gross extremities. If, in your mind it's only full-blown industrialism or going back to the woods, then I think further argument is moot and I'm done with it. I'm aware how it's hypocrisy to say to a person from the 3rd world, that we shouldn't burn as much coal and oil, that they shouldn't cut down all the forests and hunt down endangered animals. I know they'd want to send me to hell for saying things like that. Still, those things are true and the fact that those things are happening, in a large part, because how many people are eating up how much percentage of the world's income makes it even worse, because we could do MUCH better with the resources.<br /> <br /> That industrialism makes life easier doesn't mean there aren't a million problems with it and that we shouldn't strive for better. Besides, nobody said that industrialism is the devil, just that it has considerable drawbacks too and that there is a point, where you can't justify everything in the name of progress and living better, especially when that &amp;quot;living better&amp;quot; has serious dangers regarding the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you do recognize that industrialization were and IS a good thing right? Because if you think it utterly evil... Go to the woods. Don't be an hypocritical. But, if don't, it's ok. No problem thinking it could be better. It could, and it MUST. Just don't pretend that industries are the Devil, because you just happen to love them so much.<br /> <br /> So, since you LOVE industries (and you do, because you must be well fed, well clothed and well sheltered, not to mention that you can have such a commoditie as the internet. So, you truly love all that industrial world, stop denying it), you should thank the techies. Have you thanked the techies for all those luxuries yet?<br /> <br /> Look, it's ok to want changes, and to be worried about the enviroment. That's GOOD. And no, we &quot;third worlders&quot; don't wanna burn down all our woods and burn all the oil and coal that we can. But we want to develop. Its easy saying all those things and speak on behalf of the poor living in Europe. Its also easy to say that the green revolution were a bad thing like Aya said, and that 4.5 billion people he never met should starve to death, when he is living in USA with a full stomach. Its also easy to talk about how bad is the western civilization - when you're living in it. But know, if you have all that, is because of those damn industries. Is because of the &quot;opressive&quot; western civilization that you're living in. In game, it's because of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Do you try to reduce consumption? Good, that's great. Everybody should do it. We can live with less.<br /> <br /> But don't demonize everything about the western civilization, or about the modern world. You own EVERYTHING to that civilization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:03:33-08:00","id":1039772,"title":"","content":"That is a point that bares remembering. The scientific method as we know it today simply doesn't exist in WoD.<br /> <br /> When we say &quot;science&quot; it is all about reductionism and building on previously accepted principles, or trying to find logical reasons to create new principles.<br /> <br /> Deductive reasoning is still used, but it's only a tool to create a new model for the consensus. Nothing is discovered, only adapted and attached.<br /> <br /> They use language to categorise everything they see so it may be easier to pick apart and allow for more believable attempts at recreation.<br /> <br /> While real world science is about groping around in the dark and trying to print a map out of what you feel, WoD science is more like trying to creat the map as makes sense and having the darkness conform to it.<br /> <br /> But honestly, I think that's the biggest contribution the technocracy have provided. Consistency.<br /> <br /> Without the technocracy, there would be no consistency, no repeatsbility. It would be like there was no universal standards, thus people of different cultures would be unable to work together at all.<br /> <br /> If it wasn't for the order of reason, the traditions wouldn't have formed, thus giving way to a magical equivilant of consistency through communication. But what the technocracy did that the Traditions could not was to make everything, not just the terminology they used, but the practices, methods, rites, and explanations codified. And that is why they've been so successful and what mankind today doesn't need to be awakened in order to reap the benefites.<br /> <br /> The technocracy brought the masses a more consistent reality, and along with it, less incentive to ever be anything but asleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:08:55-08:00","id":1039774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039770#post1039770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And where do you think that $1 trillion went? It went to American and European banks, invested in American and European companies, buying American and European properties, and vacationing in American and European cities. It is the same thing with oligarchs all over the world, we welcome their money as long as they keep their people poor and grateful for the scraps that we leave them.<br /> <br /> America and Russia pretty much ruled the world from 1945-1991 and, since 1991, America pretty much ruled the playground by itself. Yes, China grew wealthy...off of providing America and Europe with cheap goods. Yes, India is getting wealthier...off of providing America and Europe with cheap services. It is not like they have much of a choice really though, as America has a nasty habit of assassinating leaders that will not play ball and of invading countries of leaders they cannot assassinate. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, the evil americans (which by the way, you seem to be one) will kidnap me during my sleep here in Brazil if I say shit about them on the internet. Sure.<br /> <br /> It puzzles me than, that my neighbor country CHILE here in South America, should reach the envyed place of &quot;Developed Country&quot; in the next decade, all by itself, doing nothing but giving a HUGE freedom for the economy.<br /> <br /> And I'm not seeing that many assassinations in Chile to keep them as dirty poor peasants","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:09:42-08:00","id":1039775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039762#post1039762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, what you're saying is the nonsense. Before the Order of Reason, people new their shit. Ok, that's not wrong. But it wasn't science. And it wasn't technology. Not in the WoD. The civilizations would use the maths of the proto hermetics, like the ethruscs from Rome.<br /> <br /> But there was no science.<br /> <br /> Science, in the WoD, is a result of the technocratic CONSENSUS.<br /> <br /> Before the Technocrats, diseases TRULY were caused by evil spirits.There WEREN'T microscopic pathogens back there; and there was no REAL technology. Because crystals could be used to generate light for example, without el\u00e9ctrica power. And a piece of stick could throw fireballs.<br /> <br /> In the WoD, the Order of Reason CREATED the scientific &quot;facts&quot;, it did not DISCOVERED them.<br /> <br /> So, &quot;science and technology&quot; truly are inventions of the Order of Reason and the Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest you read up the &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot; section in M20. Those things you wrote aren't either or, they're coexist and always were. I frequently had the feeling that people often misinterpret what the consensus mean.<br /> <br /> The Romans had elaborated aquaducts and baths, even floor heating. What was that, if not the application of science? What it was, if not technology? Technology isn't just computers and cars and electricity, technology is EVERY, well, technology humanity ever did. They also had a sophisticated medical knowledge, which was saved by the Middle-East and then brought back to Europe. <br /> <br /> Also, we have the signs in the ice caps that Rome made the biggest ecological footstep as pollution goes before the industrialization.<br /> <br /> During the middle ages people built amazing cathedrals with nothing but chalk, pieces of wood and, paper and coal. And with geometry, physics, mathematics and so on. Wasn't that science?<br /> <br /> You just can't ascribe everything they did and know in the old times as &quot;they knew their shit, but it wasn't science&quot;. Because, yes, it was.<br /> <br /> You know, I read Victorian sources, because I'm interested in Bartitsu. They LOVED labeling everything as &quot;scientific&quot;. They didn't really know that much more in comparison to earlier ages, but hey, it was SCIEEENCEEEEE! and that sold the product, because that was the calling of the day.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:09:48-08:00","id":1039776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, science wasn't invented nor created by the Union. They just control it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And when the ones that think that Technocracy invented science notice that science existed in a time before Technocracy was even conceived, the recour to the old Time Travel &quot;they retconned history to make it seem sicence always existed&quot;. Which, ironically, means that the &quot;unmodified history&quot; could have been a paradise ruled by benevolent Traditions solving all humanity's problems. After all, if all history has been retconned by the Tech-heads, it's no wonder than mystic seem to be the bad guys :P .<br /> But I don't think history has been retconned, I think that the technocracy it's given too much importance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:11:35-08:00","id":1039777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039769#post1039769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This it's something that I have repeated over, and over, and over, and over...<br /> <br /> There's always people that think that science was invented by the Technocracy because that's the propaganda Technocrats sell in their books. And for some reason people buys this, even when it's explicitly stated to be IOC propaganda. Like if Pythagoras would think itself as a Technocrat, if he was raised from the dead. Or like 2 of the Conventions of the Technocracy hadnt come from the Order of Hermes.<br /> <br /> No, science wasn't invented nor created by the Union. They just control it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Science isn't REALLY a thing in the WoD... IRL, science is the search for the truth, but in the WoD, it is the biggest lie ever told... Or, a necessary lie.<br /> <br /> Be it as it may, it were invented, literally, by the techies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:11:47-08:00","id":1039778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039769#post1039769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This it's something that I have repeated over, and over, and over, and over...<br /> <br /> There's always people that think that science was invented by the Technocracy because that's the propaganda Technocrats sell in their books. And for some reason people buys this, even when it's explicitly stated to be IOC propaganda. Like if Pythagoras would think itself as a Technocrat, if he was raised from the dead. Or like 2 of the Conventions of the Technocracy hadnt come from the Order of Hermes.<br /> <br /> No, science wasn't invented nor created by the Union. They just control it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And still it gets repeated. Agree, it's somewhat mind-boggling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:18:58-08:00","id":1039779,"title":"","content":"Hardly, there is no need to worry about individual citizens, it is the leaders of Brazil that my government is worried about. Anyway, concerning Chile, you forget about the assassination of Allende and the dictatorship of Pinoche, and America has been too busy kicking the Afghanis and the Iraqis to worry much about its southern neighbors since 2002. Chile is already a developed county, it has been a member of the OECD since 2010.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:21:13-08:00","id":1039780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039775#post1039775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suggest you read up the &amp;quot;Earthly Foundations&amp;quot; section in M20. Those things you wrote aren't either or, they're coexist and always were. I frequently had the feeling that people often misinterpret what the consensus mean.<br /> <br /> The Romans had elaborated aquaducts and baths, even floor heating. What was that, if not the application of science? What it was, if not technology? Technology isn't just computers and cars and electricity, technology is EVERY, well, technology humanity ever did. They also had a sophisticated medical knowledge, which was saved by the Middle-East and then brought back to Europe. <br /> <br /> Also, we have the signs in the ice caps that Rome made the biggest ecological footstep as pollution goes before the industrialization.<br /> <br /> During the middle ages people built amazing cathedrals with nothing but chalk, pieces of wood and, paper and coal. And with geometry, physics, mathematics and so on. Wasn't that science?<br /> <br /> You just can't ascribe everything they did and know in the old times as &amp;quot;they knew their shit, but it wasn't science&amp;quot;. Because, yes, it was.<br /> <br /> You know, I read Victorian sources, because I'm interested in Bartitsu. They LOVED labeling everything as &amp;quot;scientific&amp;quot;. They didn't really know that much more in comparison to earlier ages, but hey, it was SCIEEENCEEEEE! and that sold the product, because that was the calling of the day.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget, the vast majority of technological and scientific history comes to us courteousy of Technocratic Revisionism. Straight from the desk of the NWO academia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:25:51-08:00","id":1039783,"title":"","content":"And, within CWoD, the Nockers from Changeling pursued science and technology long before the creation of the Technocracy. Whether they were creating mundane or chimerical technology, their members and their kinain pursued science and technology since before the Sundering. Of course, the idea that non-humans would have influenced the creation of science and technology before the Technocracy is something that the Technocracy cannot accept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 01-28-2017, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:26:59-08:00","id":1039785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039775#post1039775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suggest you read up the &amp;quot;Earthly Foundations&amp;quot; section in M20. Those things you wrote aren't either or, they're coexist and always were. I frequently had the feeling that people often misinterpret what the consensus mean.<br /> <br /> The Romans had elaborated aquaducts and baths, even floor heating. What was that, if not the application of science? What it was, if not technology? Technology isn't just computers and cars and electricity, technology is EVERY, well, technology humanity ever did. They also had a sophisticated medical knowledge, which was saved by the Middle-East and then brought back to Europe. <br /> <br /> Also, we have the signs in the ice caps that Rome made the biggest ecological footstep as pollution goes before the industrialization.<br /> <br /> During the middle ages people built amazing cathedrals with nothing but chalk, pieces of wood and, paper and coal. And with geometry, physics, mathematics and so on. Wasn't that science?<br /> <br /> You just can't ascribe everything they did and know in the old times as &amp;quot;they knew their shit, but it wasn't science&amp;quot;. Because, yes, it was.<br /> <br /> You know, I read Victorian sources, because I'm interested in Bartitsu. They LOVED labeling everything as &amp;quot;scientific&amp;quot;. They didn't really know that much more in comparison to earlier ages, but hey, it was SCIEEENCEEEEE! and that sold the product, because that was the calling of the day.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No dude. If you were talking about the real world, yes, you would be right.<br /> <br /> But, at the time of the Romans, the very physical laws weren't the same (in the game). They used Hermetic maths, which probably means that their &quot;technology&quot; and &quot;sciences&quot; were based on things that, in the real world are absolutely bullshit, like astrology, numerology, elemental correspondence and alchemy, but in the game WERE ALL REAL (at least in that time). Hell, in the game scenario, maybe the aqueducts of Rome transported the water AGAINST THE GRAVITY VECTOR... Simply because <b>*gravity* </b> DIDNT EXIST UNTIL THE TECHIES INVENTED IT.<br /> <br /> That's what we mean with &quot;they invented it&quot;. In the WoD, science is as much an invention as eucledian geometry of the Hermetic or the healing crystals of the Verbena. It's all bullshit - numerology, psychism, parapsychology and chemistry, evolutive biology, physics, all equaly BS - or equaly true, who knows - in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:32:19-08:00","id":1039789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039771#post1039771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you do recognize that industrialization were and IS a good thing right? Because if you think it utterly evil... Go to the woods. Don't be an hypocritical. But, if don't, it's ok. No problem thinking it could be better. It could, and it MUST. Just don't pretend that industries are the Devil, because you just happen to love them so much.<br /> <br /> So, since you LOVE industries (and you do, because you must be well fed, well clothed and well sheltered, not to mention that you can have such a commoditie as the internet. So, you truly love all that industrial world, stop denying it), you should thank the techies. Have you thanked the techies for all those luxuries yet?<br /> <br /> Look, it's ok to want changes, and to be worried about the enviroment. That's GOOD. And no, we &quot;third worlders&quot; don't wanna burn down all our woods and burn all the oil and coal that we can. But we want to develop. Its easy saying all those things and speak on behalf of the poor living in Europe. Its also easy to say that the green revolution were a bad thing like Aya said, and that 4.5 billion people he never met should starve to death, when he is living in USA with a full stomach. Its also easy to talk about how bad is the western civilization - when you're living in it. But know, if you have all that, is because of those damn industries. Is because of the &quot;opressive&quot; western civilization that you're living in. In game, it's because of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Do you try to reduce consumption? Good, that's great. Everybody should do it. We can live with less.<br /> <br /> But don't demonize everything about the western civilization, or about the modern world. You own EVERYTHING to that civilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Again, you're looking at it as something black and white. Love it, or going back to the woods. Okay, if you truly believe in that, I has nothing more to say about it. There's a thing as sincere criticism of excess behavior without going to the other extreme, you know?<br /> <br /> 2. Nobody said industrialism is the true evil and that nothing good came from it. You were the only one saying that. You're pulling strawmans.<br /> <br /> 3. And<i> again,</i> the argument that in the game, civilization, especially Western civilization should just thank everything to the Union. We could argue about it all day. You think this, I don't. The books are tend to be agreeing with me (and I believe that it's even more close to reality), so I take it as the setting wasn't intended as like that. What you think is your headcannon and your version of the setting, where the Technocracy is in the right.<br /> <br /> Actually, I'm marveled again and again at how brilliant it is. &quot;Do you like everything which is good and comfy in your lives? Do you like your health, your job, your safety? Your children's safety? Well, all of that is just because of US. Because we provide it, because we're defending you. Meanwhile, do you see those other guys? They want to tear it down and take it away, and send you back to the woods, to be the prey of the night, just because they're selfish and aren't capable of thinking about anyone, but themselves. Oh, that we have immoral methods and having control over your life and have our own selfish bastards pulling the strings? Noooop, move over, there's nothing to see. Eat your McKiller. Good boy.&quot;<br /> <br /> I know the later part is going into Tradition-propaganda territory, but that's it: we could go either way. It's just, that somehow, pro-technocratic people are tend to go more frequently to their extreme and taking it as the truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:44:33-08:00","id":1039797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Science isn't REALLY a thing in the WoD... IRL, science is the search for the truth, but in the WoD, it is the biggest lie ever told... Or, a necessary lie.<br /> <br /> Be it as it may, it were invented, literally, by the techies<br /> <br /> But, at the time of the Romans, the very physical laws weren't the same (in the game). They used Hermetic maths, which probably means that their &quot;technology&quot; and &quot;sciences&quot; were based on things that, in the real world are absolutely bullshit, like astrology, numerology, elemental correspondence and alchemy, but in the game WERE ALL REAL (at least in that time). Hell, in the game scenario, maybe the aqueducts of Rome transported the water AGAINST THE GRAVITY VECTOR... Simply because <b>*gravity* </b> DIDNT EXIST UNTIL THE TECHIES INVENTED IT.<br /> <br /> That's what we mean with &quot;they invented it&quot;. In the WoD, science is as much an invention as eucledian geometry of the Hermetic or the healing crystals of the Verbena. It's all bullshit - numerology, psychism, parapsychology and chemistry, evolutive biology, physics, all equaly BS - or equaly true, who knows - in the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have already argumented this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And when the ones that think that Technocracy invented science notice that science existed in a time before Technocracy was even conceived, the recour to the old Time Travel &quot;they retconned history to make it seem sicence always existed&quot;. Which, ironically, means that the &quot;unmodified history&quot; could have been a paradise ruled by benevolent Traditions solving all humanity's problems. After all, if all history has been retconned by the Tech-heads, it's no wonder than mystic seem to be the bad guys :P .<br /> But I don't think history has been retconned, I think that the technocracy it's given too much importance.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, either science always existed, or it's irrelevant to the matter of the merits of a technocratic world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-28-2017, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:44:48-08:00","id":1039798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039785#post1039785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No dude. If you were talking about the real world, yes, you would be right.<br /> <br /> But, at the time of the Romans, the very physical laws weren't the same (in the game). They used Hermetic maths, which probably means that their &quot;technology&quot; and &quot;sciences&quot; were based on things that, in the real world are absolutely bullshit, like astrology, numerology, elemental correspondence and alchemy, but in the game WERE ALL REAL (at least in that time). Hell, in the game scenario, maybe the aqueducts of Rome transported the water AGAINST THE GRAVITY VECTOR... Simply because <b>*gravity* </b> DIDNT EXIST UNTIL THE TECHIES INVENTED IT.<br /> <br /> That's what we mean with &quot;they invented it&quot;. In the WoD, science is as much an invention as eucledian geometry of the Hermetic or the healing crystals of the Verbena. It's all bullshit - numerology, psychism, parapsychology and chemistry, evolutive biology, physics, all equaly BS - or equaly true, who knows - in the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, dude, that I admittedly didn't read all the books (working on it), but I didn't read, even in the books about the Hermetics, that regular mathematics and science didn't work back in the day. More like it coexisted with magic, because even during the high mythic age you couldn't do things on the scale like the aquaducts only with magic. They'd just eaten up too much constant energy to maintain. As far as I'm aware of, the marvels of earlier ages are still exist in WoD and I read it nowhere that the Roman Hermetics built the Colosseum, or that Medieval Choristers built the cathedrals only with magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:49:38-08:00","id":1039802,"title":"","content":"You can play at the Dark Ages (DA Mage), and science worked as well as ever (even if it was less developed).<br /> <br /> And before answering about retconned history, read my previous post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:50:50-08:00","id":1039804,"title":"","content":"Just a reminder that 'science existed before the technocracy' is more or less meaningless. Science as we recognize it stems largely from later than the Order of Reason's foundation, and what stems from before is usually of Middle Eastern origin, where one of the OoR's antecedents, the Mokteshaf al-Nour, were operative. For the rest, you can place the blame/praise squarely on the Hermetic tradition, as just like in real life, they were doing vaguely sciency things (yes, even as they were doing astrology they did astronomy; even as they did numerology, they did mathematics. You can't actually do numerology <i>without</i> mundane mathematics, by the way.) for a long, long time before 'science' caught on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T21:11:42-08:00","id":1039811,"title":"","content":"China and India had mathematics and technology long before the founding of the Order of Reason. Chinese and Indian mathematics and technology probably predate Sumer, though you start getting into mythology rather than history that far back. Heck, there is some evidence that China and India had agriculture, one of the first 'advanced' technologies, thousands of years before it was inventing in the Middle East, as early as 9,000 BCE, though there is some disagreement in the archeological community concerning those claims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T21:47:51-08:00","id":1039819,"title":"","content":"None of which are what we would call 'science'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T21:53:23-08:00","id":1039820,"title":"","content":"But it was technology, which some of the previous people suggested did not exist before the Technocrats. Heck, fire starting is a technology and it dates back to nearly 2 million years ago with the evidence a regularly cooked foods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T21:56:24-08:00","id":1039821,"title":"","content":"Sure, but my post was concerned only with science. Also, by that definition of technology - the formal, non-colloquial one- magic is also a technology in a world where it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T22:21:54-08:00","id":1039825,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that the Order of Reason has been around since the Roman Empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T22:23:37-08:00","id":1039826,"title":"","content":"The Order of Reason has <i>not</i> been around since the Roman Empire by any stretch, unless you mean to include the Eastern Roman Empire/Byzantium in the definition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T22:37:02-08:00","id":1039828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039798#post1039798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, dude, that I admittedly didn't read all the books (working on it), but I didn't read, even in the books about the Hermetics, that regular mathematics and science didn't work back in the day. More like it coexisted with magic, because even during the high mythic age you couldn't do things on the scale like the aquaducts only with magic. They'd just eaten up too much constant energy to maintain. As far as I'm aware of, the marvels of earlier ages are still exist in WoD and I read it nowhere that the Roman Hermetics built the Colosseum, or that Medieval Choristers built the cathedrals only with magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the settings of WoD, your TV, computer, car, all that is &quot;magic&quot;. No, the hermetics didn't built Rome with lights from the skies. <br /> <br /> But<br /> <br /> Everything were made of water, fire, earth and air<br /> Astrology was VITAL<br /> Looking the insides of an animal would tell you the future.<br /> <br /> People were not &quot;bound&quot; in the floor because of gravity. It simply were the will of the gods. Maths were always maths, the Hermetic love it until today. But physical laws? They began with Newton. Before that, it were the will of the Gods (that mostly live in the High Umbra). And it were absolutely true; if the god-that-keeps-us-on-the-flor got angry, he would make the person float around in the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T22:47:18-08:00","id":1039832,"title":"","content":"No, Aristotle was the first person to speculate on the nature of gravity, and he attributed it to the 'love' (an inexact translation, but it will work for now) between an object and the Earth. He considered that each element had different amounts of gravity and, in order from highest to lowest, they were Earth, Water, Air, Fire, and Aether. Oh, and Aristotle was pretty much one of the first scientists (as we understand the term), though it could be argued that Democritus (the person who first thought up atomic theory, alien life, and the idea of the Milky Way as a collection of stars) may have been the first scientist (and both of them were atheists who were skeptical of magic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T23:00:51-08:00","id":1039839,"title":"","content":"Democritus was a philosopher, not a scientist. He did not base his theories on evidence, tests, or reproducibility, but on logic without a backing of evidence or mathematical proofs. That is an enormous, and important difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T23:04:46-08:00","id":1039840,"title":"","content":"He did biological and mineral experiments, though I agree that his thoughts on astronomy and physics were based on logic rather than experiments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T23:19:44-08:00","id":1039845,"title":"","content":"Merely performing an experiment does not make a scientist. The method is what does, and it postdates Democritus by quite a ways even in its Hermetic forebear. This is one of the things that complicates any such discussion. Science is actually several things we colloquially lump together, some of which have very little to do with what science actually is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:08:17-08:00","id":1040026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039832#post1039832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Aristotle was the first person to speculate on the nature of gravity, and he attributed it to the 'love' (an inexact translation, but it will work for now) between an object and the Earth. He considered that each element had different amounts of gravity and, in order from highest to lowest, they were Earth, Water, Air, Fire, and Aether. Oh, and Aristotle was pretty much one of the first scientists (as we understand the term), though it could be argued that Democritus (the person who first thought up atomic theory, alien life, and the idea of the Milky Way as a collection of stars) may have been the first scientist (and both of them were atheists who were skeptical of magic).</div> </div> </div> </div>So, that means that things were attached to the soil due their &quot;affinity&quot; to earth, water, air and fire. In the times of Rome, a person with too much &quot;fire&quot; on her, would LITERALLY weight less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:26:01-08:00","id":1040035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1039832#post1039832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Aristotle was the first person to speculate on the nature of gravity, and he attributed it to the 'love' (an inexact translation, but it will work for now) between an object and the Earth. He considered that each element had different amounts of gravity and, in order from highest to lowest, they were Earth, Water, Air, Fire, and Aether. Oh, and Aristotle was pretty much one of the first scientists (as we understand the term), though it could be argued that Democritus (the person who first thought up atomic theory, alien life, and the idea of the Milky Way as a collection of stars) may have been the first scientist (and both of them were atheists who were skeptical of magic).</div> </div> </div> </div>Aristotle gets no points for this speculation on why things fall down because his explanation is 100% wrong and far removed from anything we might know today as &quot;gravity&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:29:43-08:00","id":1040040,"title":"","content":"Newton didn't understand the nature of gravity either, he just mathematically described it, so does he lose science points because he did not understand curved space?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:47:07-08:00","id":1040053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040040#post1040040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Newton didn't understand the nature of gravity either, he just mathematically described it, so does he lose science points because he did not understand curved space?</div> </div> </div> </div>Newton's theory explains things which are largely true and provides a functional mathematical model for describing the world. Aristotle's &quot;things are made out of fire, water, earth and air and each of those elements longs to its natural place in the world&quot; doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:49:20-08:00","id":1040055,"title":"","content":"Aristotle also stated as facts things that could easily be disproven by observation. Although, perhaps heavier things really did fall faster in his time. Consensus only knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T11:34:59-08:00","id":1040116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040026#post1040026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, that means that things were attached to the soil due their &quot;affinity&quot; to earth, water, air and fire. In the times of Rome, a person with too much &quot;fire&quot; on her, would LITERALLY weight less.</div> </div> </div> </div>That lends an eerie context to the whole &quot;She was a fiery woman.&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:11:29-08:00","id":1040131,"title":"","content":"Again, Earthly Foundations. Some things just are just the way the World IS. Not everything is or were defined by the consensus.<br /> <br /> From M20:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Earthly Foundations: Certain laws of Earth\u2019s reality<br /> physics are more or less fixed. You can go against them,<br /> but no matter who you are or what you do, those efforts<br /> will almost certainly count as vulgar magick.<br /> \u2022 Technocratic Reality: Here, the laws of scientific<br /> technology dictate what is and is not acceptable within<br /> the zone.<br /> <br /> There's a quite a big difference between the two and most things that came up as results of the technocratic consensus is in fact more of a Foundation, regardless of what people believed in the past. Like things falling and water flowing downward.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:14:12-08:00","id":1040133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040131#post1040131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, Earthly Foundations. Some things just are just the way the World IS. Not everything is or were defined by the consensus.<br /> <br /> From M20:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Earthly Foundations: Certain laws of Earth\u2019s reality<br /> physics are more or less fixed. You can go against them,<br /> but no matter who you are or what you do, those efforts<br /> will almost certainly count as vulgar magick.<br /> \u2022 Technocratic Reality: Here, the laws of scientific<br /> technology dictate what is and is not acceptable within<br /> the zone.<br /> <br /> There's a quite a big difference between the two and most things that came up as results of the technocratic consensus is in fact more of a Foundation, regardless of what people believed in the past. Like things falling and water flowing downward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that this is referring to how Reality Zones operate today.<br /> <br /> Perhaps in the distant past things were much less fixed. Perhaps it was possible for water to flow upwards back then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:33:38-08:00","id":1040141,"title":"","content":"Except, that nothing in the book says that those things weren't like that in the past. On the contrary, everything indicates that those Foundations are in fact the baseline of reality and always worked the same way.<br /> <br /> Also from M20:<br /> <br /> &quot;Some things are almost always vulgar, no matter who\u2019s<br /> doing them, where they\u2019re doing them, or how they\u2019re being<br /> done. In game terms, acts that violate these Earthly Foundations<br /> contradict the baseline reality for Earth.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;\u2022 Obvious violations of normal physical laws: Water<br /> running uphill, people flying around, free-floating<br /> molecules abruptly manifesting as solid mass, turtles<br /> suddenly moving at cheetah speed\u2026 such gross alterations<br /> of Earth\u2019s primary physical laws tend to incur Paradox.<br /> Certain long-term projects \u2013 like airplanes, flying<br /> ointments, and martial arts \u2013 might be able to bend<br /> those principles a bit, but the act of investing that much<br /> time, energy, and devotion to a task still recognizes that<br /> those principles exist. Simply ignoring them \u2013 say, by<br /> jumping off a roof while believing you can fly \u2013 is a good<br /> way to get your ass kicked, either by Paradox (if you do<br /> fly) or by physics (if you don\u2019t).&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> That's why I'm saying that the Consensus gets misinterpreted again and again. NOT everything is the product of Consensus or local Reality Zones in earlier ages. Some thing are just how the World works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:40:05-08:00","id":1040150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040141#post1040141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, that nothing in the book says that those things weren't like that in the past. On the contrary, everything indicates that those Foundations are in fact the baseline of reality and always worked the same way.<br /> <br /> Also from M20:<br /> <br /> &quot;Some things are almost always vulgar, no matter who\u2019s<br /> doing them, where they\u2019re doing them, or how they\u2019re being<br /> done. In game terms, acts that violate these Earthly Foundations<br /> contradict the baseline reality for Earth.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;\u2022 Obvious violations of normal physical laws: Water<br /> running uphill, people flying around, free-floating<br /> molecules abruptly manifesting as solid mass, turtles<br /> suddenly moving at cheetah speed\u2026 such gross alterations<br /> of Earth\u2019s primary physical laws tend to incur Paradox.<br /> Certain long-term projects \u2013 like airplanes, flying<br /> ointments, and martial arts \u2013 might be able to bend<br /> those principles a bit, but the act of investing that much<br /> time, energy, and devotion to a task still recognizes that<br /> those principles exist. Simply ignoring them \u2013 say, by<br /> jumping off a roof while believing you can fly \u2013 is a good<br /> way to get your ass kicked, either by Paradox (if you do<br /> fly) or by physics (if you don\u2019t).&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> That's why I'm saying that the Consensus gets misinterpreted again and again. NOT everything is the product of Consensus or local Reality Zones in earlier ages. Some thing are just how the World works.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what makes this stuff consistent if not humans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:51:26-08:00","id":1040158,"title":"","content":"Gaia? The Universe? Reality? Not everything is about humans and the Universe existed tens of billions of years before humanity fell from the trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:56:37-08:00","id":1040159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040150#post1040150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what makes this stuff consistent if not humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Insert whatever creation story, or theory you like.<br /> <br /> It's simple physics. It's the Triad/Gaia. It's God. We don't know how the Universe came into being and why it works the way it works. We just know it simply operates along certain rules, but humans could mess with those rules and the weight of the consensus/reality zones could impose additional rules over it, or loosen up certain rules to a degree.<br /> <br /> Or what do you think, how things worked before the Consensus? Was it a world like Ravenloft, where bubbles of different realities floated in a sea of astral fog? How travel worked?<br /> <br /> I suspect that's why people say that Mage and the Consensus is incompatible with other games, because they keep misinterpreting it as the Consensus defines everything.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:05:46-08:00","id":1040162,"title":"","content":"I'd be a Hermetic. I was a history major. I get the links between real world Hermetic traditions and the foundations of both modern Western Science and Western Democracy. So, I'm a Trad Mage all the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:11:33-08:00","id":1040165,"title":"","content":"The Consensus is an artifact of human belief that allows the Mages of the Union to make their magic coincidental when the Foundations of Reality would make it vulgar (it is also a weapon created by the Union to commit genocide against supernatural creatures that lack sufficient durability to resist its effects). The Consensus overlays the Foundations of Reality, it does not replace them. The Foundations of Reality are what allow the mundane and supernatural worlds to exist and Paradox, in many ways, is the objection of Reality to having its Foundations violated (the Consensus is an amazing construct because it insulates certain Mages from the objections of Reality, so the Consensus functions as a low grade Quiet for the entire Union).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:15:00-08:00","id":1040169,"title":"","content":"It is entirely possible that Earthly Foundations are things that are incredibly deeply buried in human expectation. Think about it this way your knowledge of how things like cars, bullets, electricity etc starts from when you are old enough to start learning about them. Your knowledge about gravity, object permanence, your own motion, etc. starts from the day you are born because that is a part of learning how to move. You can change the way you think about them, learn exceptions about them, even accept that they are situational, but you would outright panic if they stopped working and you didn't know why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:28:20-08:00","id":1040176,"title":"","content":"That's a nice theory, but it doesn't explain what was before humanity. Moreover, nothing in the books I read indicates that, in fact, quite the contrary (see above).<br /> <br /> Aya, yeah, the Consensus is a world-wide reality zone,which makes certain kinds of magic easier for certain people. It's entirely possible that it makes certain non-magical things more stable, according to that paradigm. Planes might crash more frequently without it, for example. But the Consensus largely made technomagic more coincidental, not technologies based on baseline reality possible. Those would work without it. <br /> <br /> For example modern medicine, based on knowledge about bacteria and such. Sorry, those things worked before the consensus, animals got sick, decomposition worked the same, etc. It wasn't all just spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:33:18-08:00","id":1040179,"title":"","content":"Yes, I agree. The Consensus is a human artifact that modifies Reality rather than being Reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:45:30-08:00","id":1040188,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I can get behind that. It also makes it fit in with WTA a bit better. Everything consistent is the act of the Weaver. yadda yadda yadda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:12:31-08:00","id":1040208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040141#post1040141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, that nothing in the book says that those things weren't like that in the past. On the contrary, everything indicates that those Foundations are in fact the baseline of reality and always worked the same way.<br /> <br /> Also from M20:<br /> <br /> &quot;Some things are almost always vulgar, no matter who\u2019s<br /> doing them, where they\u2019re doing them, or how they\u2019re being<br /> done. In game terms, acts that violate these Earthly Foundations<br /> contradict the baseline reality for Earth.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;\u2022 Obvious violations of normal physical laws: Water<br /> running uphill, people flying around, free-floating<br /> molecules abruptly manifesting as solid mass, turtles<br /> suddenly moving at cheetah speed\u2026 such gross alterations<br /> of Earth\u2019s primary physical laws tend to incur Paradox.<br /> Certain long-term projects \u2013 like airplanes, flying<br /> ointments, and martial arts \u2013 might be able to bend<br /> those principles a bit, but the act of investing that much<br /> time, energy, and devotion to a task still recognizes that<br /> those principles exist. Simply ignoring them \u2013 say, by<br /> jumping off a roof while believing you can fly \u2013 is a good<br /> way to get your ass kicked, either by Paradox (if you do<br /> fly) or by physics (if you don\u2019t).&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> That's why I'm saying that the Consensus gets misinterpreted again and again. NOT everything is the product of Consensus or local Reality Zones in earlier ages. Some thing are just how the World works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, Earthly foundations are an optional rule, and also essentially an excuse to throw stupid and largely arbitrary limitations.<br /> <br /> Like &quot;You can't turn vampires into lawn chairs&quot; for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:28:21-08:00","id":1040212,"title":"","content":"sorry, double post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-29-2017, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:28:35-08:00","id":1040213,"title":"","content":"They are necessary if you want to have a workable crossover game. If you want to go ahead and create an alternative system that works as well in crossover games and explains Reality before human existence, go ahead, no one will stop you. And I agree, if you can find specific rules (not fluff) that contradicts Earthly Foundations, please share it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:34:57-08:00","id":1040216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040208#post1040208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Firstly, Earthly foundations are an optional rule,</div> </div> </div> </div>EVERYTHING in M20 is optional and it got stressed frequently. However, there are certain things that the book presents as the default.<br /> <br /> My opinion is that Earthly Foundations makes the setting a LOT more plausible and better-working with other splats. But that's just my opinion, you have every right to disagree with it.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, I'd like to repeat: cite passages from earlier books which contradict the Earthly Foundations concept. Again, I admit I didn't read everything, but nothing I read suggested things people are claiming there. I'm still on the opinion that the majority of the &quot;the Consensus is everything&quot; approach is largely people's headcannon and personal interpretation of the setting, not the setting as it was written and I saw nothing so far that contradicts it. I suspect the Earthly Foundations in M20 is just the explicitly written form of how writers treated it in the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and also essentially an excuse to throw stupid and largely arbitrary limitations.<br /> <br /> Like &quot;You can't turn vampires into lawn chairs&quot; for example. </div> </div> </div>Well, I guess if you like to play a game where mages are stupidly powerful, even more than otherwise and all other splats are irrelevant...<br /> <br /> On my part, I like mages to be powerful, but having limitations and I like the idea of a functioning, humanity-independent world better than the idea of a big, mutual dream, where everything is just the result of human minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:51:44-08:00","id":1040221,"title":"","content":"I agree. The setting has Changelings and the Dreaming if you want to have that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T15:12:25-08:00","id":1040239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040040#post1040040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Newton didn't understand the nature of gravity either, he just mathematically described it, so does he lose science points because he did not understand curved space?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a tremendous difference between noting a natural thing and spitballing ideas about it or noting a natural thing, sitting down, figuring it out, testing your assumptions, and finding a mathematical proof that explains what you're seeing, discarding ideas that don't make the cut of evidence or that cannot be proofed out. One is, in essence, a wild guess (even if a very precise one) - the other involves at least a proto-scientific method.<br /> <br /> Let me put it this way. If I, the bizarre wizard man that I am, notice the sun rises and set, and determine that the sun is in fact a great hurtling fire that pursues the lake that comes out when it is hiding, and from there also deduce (quite logically, with that as a base parameter) that during the waning days the moon is evaporating as water exposed to flame does, and that these waters coalesce again during the waxing, and that therefore the moon is closer to the sun during the new moon than the full moon, and also determine that this is why the tides are higher in the full moon (as the moon, a giant ocean not having evaporated, is sympathetically linked to the seas of the earth), without repeatedly testing my ideas, am I doing science?<br /> <br /> If, however, I notice the sun rises and sets and a correlation with the tides, sit down, and try and figure it out - unsuccessfully, even, because let's say I don't comprehend gravity - and manage to determine a relationship between the heights of the tide and the stage of the moon, and then create a model that can predict that relationship and attempts to explain it, then repeatedly test that model to see if it holds up, am I doing science?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T15:19:32-08:00","id":1040241,"title":"","content":"Boy this thing went off the rails into one of the old Mage-forum-chestnuts.<br /> <br /> I'll reiterate something from previous threads about this stuff:<br /> <br /> Reality Zones are an invention of the Order of Reason. Before the rise of the Order of Reason - as seen in DA Mage - reality just was. Mages didn't think about Consensus or things like that. Nobody was fighting for how to shape reality itself. The &quot;Consensus&quot; of the time was essentially just the human experience of observing what M20 calls the Earthly Foundations (which is not something M20 invented by the way, such elements were discussed in previous books). Stuff falls down, there's a pattern of celestial movement, etc. and nobody's specific beliefs were powerful enough to actually do anything. The sun didn't orbit around the Earth in some places, while the Earth orbited around the sun in others. Much like we actually know now, they simply moved in relation to each other and everything else is a frame of reference.<br /> <br /> The Order of Reason were the ones that figured out Reality was malleable with the power of mass belief as they searched for ways to strike back at the entrenched magical societies that they saw as moral hazards. They worked to &quot;break&quot; the previous &quot;natural&quot; Reality by influencing beliefs to influence Reality via Consensus. This created Reality Zones as dominant local beliefs started to take hold (see: Sorcerer's Crusade) instead of the previous state of things. Then the Order of Reason began their efforts to unify Reality Zones through their methodology to create the modern nearly-global Consensus.<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Also remember that due to the Mage metaphysics, the Anthropic Principle is an absolute necessity. The very idea of Earthly Foundations is to establish the setting elements necessary to justify the Anthropic Principle working.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T16:42:28-08:00","id":1040286,"title":"","content":"Yes, but it still stands, that the majority, or at least a significant part of how the world works is part of the Earthly Foundations. The Consensus and reality zones in general don't override those, instead they're adding another layer to them, another set of rules.<br /> <br /> Like, flying.<br /> <br /> Humans don't fly, that's a Foundation at this stage of our evolution.<br /> <br /> Although, other things are able to fly, and using the same laws, derived from the Foundations, humans could build machines that could fly. This is still not the product of the Consensus.<br /> <br /> However, the Consensus adds another layer, that says, because of millions of indoctrinated people, that flying is <i>in fact </i>the safest method of transport, so glitches occur least frequently. The consensus also makes modes of flying, like jetpacks less vulgar, because people got accustomed to the idea that machines and science could do crazy things for real and so, it works easier, despite that it contradicts the Foundations (read, basic physical laws). However, the average modern people would have a harder time believing the dude chanting magical words and then going airborne, or suddenly sprouting wings with a 6 meters span. The point is: planes don't fly because of the consensus and the World in general doesn't work only on the base of Consensus. Also, Consensus isn't omnipotent, it doesn't overrides the Foundations, it adds to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-29-2017, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T18:50:43-08:00","id":1040354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040286#post1040286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but it still stands, that the majority, or at least a significant part of how the world works is part of the Earthly Foundations. The Consensus and reality zones in general don't override those, instead they're adding another layer to them, another set of rules.<br /> <br /> Like, flying.<br /> <br /> Humans don't fly, that's a Foundation at this stage of our evolution.<br /> <br /> Although, other things are able to fly, and using the same laws, derived from the Foundations, humans could build machines that could fly. This is still not the product of the Consensus.<br /> <br /> However, the Consensus adds another layer, that says, because of millions of indoctrinated people, that flying is <i>in fact </i>the safest method of transport, so glitches occur least frequently. The consensus also makes modes of flying, like jetpacks less vulgar, because people got accustomed to the idea that machines and science could do crazy things for real and so, it works easier, despite that it contradicts the Foundations (read, basic physical laws). However, the average modern people would have a harder time believing the dude chanting magical words and then going airborne, or suddenly sprouting wings with a 6 meters span. The point is: planes don't fly because of the consensus and the World in general doesn't work only on the base of Consensus. Also, Consensus isn't omnipotent, it doesn't overrides the Foundations, it adds to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that it doesn't. A plane in the 19th century WOULDN'T fly at all, period. Why? Consensus. People believed it to be impossible. And at that period, the Order of Reason were changing to the Union and taking a firm grip of reality.<br /> <br /> In the setting of Mage, airplanes are fully magikal machines that defies gravity. Period. It doesn't work on different air pression; it works because people believe that those huge metal birds can do it. If people stop believing that... Those planes will explode in a beautiful Paradox effect.<br /> <br /> So, those 'Earthly Foundations&quot; may just be the result of the Consensus prior to the OoR. People expected to see stuff falling, because thats how their experiences thought them. Until some giant metal birds changed that perception... Changing reality along it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T19:08:46-08:00","id":1040366,"title":"","content":"But the Earthly Foundations existed before Mages because the Rokea, Mokole, and Ananasi predate humanity and do not seem to remember anything too odd (relatively speaking).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T19:11:38-08:00","id":1040369,"title":"","content":"Consensual reality falls apart when you take a crossline view, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T19:12:42-08:00","id":1040370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040176#post1040176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a nice theory, but it doesn't explain what was before humanity. Moreover, nothing in the books I read indicates that, in fact, quite the contrary (see above).<br /> <br /> Aya, yeah, the Consensus is a world-wide reality zone,which makes certain kinds of magic easier for certain people. It's entirely possible that it makes certain non-magical things more stable, according to that paradigm. Planes might crash more frequently without it, for example. But the Consensus largely made technomagic more coincidental, not technologies based on baseline reality possible. Those would work without it.<br /> <br /> For example modern medicine, based on knowledge about bacteria and such. Sorry, those things worked before the consensus, animals got sick, decomposition worked the same, etc. It wasn't all just spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>NOTHING was before humanity. Obviously. Why would you need to explain what was 'before' humanity? In the scientific sense, what was 'before' humanity is what the Technocracy tells you. Because history is written by the victors. They've convinced everyone that dinosaurs existed and so they did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T19:13:47-08:00","id":1040373,"title":"","content":"Hm, how did humanity start then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T19:16:32-08:00","id":1040375,"title":"","content":"They were created. Just like every universe was created by a sufficiently powerful being from a higher universe. At least in Mage anyway. Now, how did THAT universe come to be? Who knows? One of those mysteries.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T19:34:22-08:00","id":1040378,"title":"","content":"The 'proper' answer, in so far as there <i>can</i> be one for Mage, is that the human being is really nothing more than another incarnated spirit that has chosen to inhabit the Umbral realm known as the 'physical' world, stemming from the same well spring as the rest of the cosmos; namely, the Unity, which splintered and crystallized into the cosmos as mages know it, generating all things within according to certain metaphysical and physical laws. All came from the Unity, all returns to the Unity, and on and on it goes. From there, it's a matter of either guided evolution (wherein higher spiritual entities that oversee certain physical laws steer creation to achieve the creation of man, the creature able to reunite the dispersed Unity into one singularity) or of simple natural laws (of course, the guided evolution by the overseers is in fact the same thing, but it depends on how one wishes to view it) for mankind to arise from the small furry mammals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T22:44:54-08:00","id":1040443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040369#post1040369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consensual reality falls apart when you take a crossline view, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, rather, it shows that, albeit it's an interesting concept and perfectly viable for individual chronicles, the game itself assumes a different view, because it acknowledges crossovers and other supernatural creatures. <br /> <br /> When you starting to leave out parts of the game and setting, because it contradicts your vision of the setting, that's the breaking point, IMO, where you went into homebrew territory instead of using the official setting as it was written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T23:01:33-08:00","id":1040452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040443#post1040443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or, rather, it shows that, albeit it's an interesting concept and perfectly viable for individual chronicles, the game itself assumes a different view, because it acknowledges crossovers and other supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> When you starting to leave out parts of the game and setting, because it contradicts your vision of the setting, that's the breaking point, IMO, where you went into homebrew territory instead of using the official setting as it was written.</div> </div> </div> </div>I maintain the rule of Primacy, myself. That rule is simple: Whatever game line you're running, it's correct and anything that contradicts is wrong, and IMO that's more or less how the game lines are intended to be viewed - even when there's a crossover supplement, there's usually a note about 'whichever line you're running should probably take precedence'. It's only when you try and treat every gameline as absolutely true and all extant together that you run into issues with basic setting concepts falling apart (not to mention setting inconsistencies out the wazoo), though admittedly Consensus Reality was never properly defined, always hazy, and more than a little self-contradictory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T23:54:42-08:00","id":1040463,"title":"","content":"There's probably more fans of the traditions out there than there are fans of the union, they may just not be speaking out so much lately. <br /> <br /> Remember that the new convention books coming out and depicting the technocracy in a new way won the technocracy a lot of fans, I too found myself having a new appreciation for it after reading the new books.<br /> <br /> The new books really boosted the fan base but aside from that, there's an underlying reason why a lot of people like the union, they use technology in their daily lives and aren't too hot on organized religion, the tradions have a big tie to organized religions and the union has an even bigger tie to technology, this makes a lot of people inherently biased towards liking the union and this is just one aspect of the tip of the iceberg.<br /> <br /> I love the freedom and power that technology has given me, I don't like the way most organized religions use to control society (and still do to a lesser extent) so I am, like it or not, a technocracy sympathizer.<br /> <br /> But I still like the traditions better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T00:02:09-08:00","id":1040468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040463#post1040463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the freedom and power that technology has given me, I don't like the way most organized religions use to control society (and still do to a lesser extent) so I am, like it or not, a technocracy sympathizer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure? The most powerful force for oppressive, brutish and controlling organized religion was not the Celestial Chorus, but the Cabal of Pure Thought and the Messianic Voices, who split into the CPT and the Chouer Celeste in due time.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:29:51-08:00","id":1040656,"title":"","content":"It should be noted, the Order of Reason (and, when it formed, the Technocracy) was responsible for the centuries long genocide against the Native Americans just because they were in the way. I think one of the reasons why they killed of the Craftmasons was that the Craftmasons were complaining too much about the genocides in the genocides in the Americas (the spread of diseases enhances to resist native forms of magic were a form of genocide).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:35:08-08:00","id":1040659,"title":"","content":"To answer the question, I've always played Tradition Mages, mainly because I can't wrap my head around how Technocratic Mages actually do their magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12903-gangrel_reaper","name":"Gangrel_Reaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T08:16:58-08:00","id":1040674,"title":"","content":"My preferred choice is Traditions Mages. I do like playing Technocrats as well, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T08:24:05-08:00","id":1040676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040656#post1040656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be noted, the Order of Reason (and, when it formed, the Technocracy) was responsible for the centuries long genocide against the Native Americans just because they were in the way. I think one of the reasons why they killed of the Craftmasons was that the Craftmasons were complaining too much about the genocides in the genocides in the Americas (the spread of diseases enhances to resist native forms of magic were a form of genocide).</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this written?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T08:39:40-08:00","id":1040689,"title":"","content":"Who else was in control of the European powers during the Age of Exploration? Does anyony really think that the OoR would not have been elbow deep in the colonization of the Americas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T09:32:49-08:00","id":1040716,"title":"","content":"I'd put (part of) the blame on the Nephandi / Reasonphandi, perhaps. From <i>Infernalism - the Path of Screams</i> :<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Celestial masters crave the gospel of the stars. They cannot learn enough about the mysteries high above them, and eagerly pursue any scrap of knowledge about the distant spheres. Although they take their names from the entrance to the Underworld, the Gatekeepers of Ganzir know old secrets of the stars. Like their forefathers, who worked within the Egyptian courts, these descendants of Babylon offer bastard versions of their lore to some Celestial Masters.<br /> A pity so many Masters soon go insane, don't you agree?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Although most K'llasshaa are filty degenerates, some of their recent &quot;converts&quot; hail from the refined halls of the Order of Reason, and bring an eerie stability.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Wyrmish Nephandi or Reasonphandi might be a possibility, as well - the Eater-of-Souls was almost summoned in the North America, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though it might have been solely work of the Order of Reason. The plagues might have been created solely by Cosians, and other members of OoR promoted anti-Native sentiments and commanded during battles and conflicts. And of course killed or neutralized local Nightfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:32:50-08:00","id":1040782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040689#post1040689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who else was in control of the European powers during the Age of Exploration? Does anyony really think that the OoR would not have been elbow deep in the colonization of the Americas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most likely the Void Engineers by the way of the NWO, since exploration is their thing. Also the Syndicate since colonization was seen as an economic thing for Europe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T12:15:26-08:00","id":1040808,"title":"","content":"Part of the reason the Americas could even be colonized was plague. It was intentionally spread in some cases, but in many others we don't know what the diseases even were or how they got there. Could the Order of Reason be behind that? Yes, but overall it doesn't fit with their goals as much as conversion does. <br /> <br /> Now, Mages don't have to be behind those plagues at all, but if they were I'd say the Nephandi are the most likely.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T12:46:34-08:00","id":1040820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040463#post1040463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's probably more fans of the traditions out there than there are fans of the union, they may just not be speaking out so much lately.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree and I might add that they're just less apparent and active on the forums.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember that the new convention books coming out and depicting the technocracy in a new way won the technocracy a lot of fans, I too found myself having a new appreciation for it after reading the new books. </div> </div> </div>People always say that, but I don't know. Ok, I read the NWO one and parts of the VE one. The NWO one, I found them after that no better, on the contrary. Probably it played into it, that I read it as someone who didn't like the Union from the get-go, but the book didn't convinced me to change my opinion. I'm honestly curious how many anti-Technocracy players thought after those books that they're in fact sympathetic. I somewhat suspect it's more like the Hollow Ones book, if you liked the concept, but had problems with the implementation, the books might succeed to shed a new, more nuanced light into it and thus making them better, but if you didn't like the concept at all, then the books won't change that. But it's an interesting topic, it would be good to hear other people's different experiences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The new books really boosted the fan base but aside from that, there's an underlying reason why a lot of people like the union, they use technology in their daily lives and aren't too hot on organized religion, the tradions have a big tie to organized religions and the union has an even bigger tie to technology, this makes a lot of people inherently biased towards liking the union and this is just one aspect of the tip of the iceberg. </div> </div> </div>I suspect that this is the biggest part and it connects to the prevalence on forums. Most people on the forums are probably science and technology-minded people, with strong feelings toward modern concepts (dare I say, &quot;The Amercian Way&quot;? I don't mean it as a snide, but it has positive and negative implications) and the Technocracy could represent that. However:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I love the freedom and power that technology has given me, I don't like the way most organized religions use to control society (and still do to a lesser extent) so I am, like it or not, a technocracy sympathizer.<br /> <br /> But I still like the traditions better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I don't like organized religion either. Never did, never will. I'm not a religious person at all. But I never saw the traditions just as organized religions, at least not the entirety of it. However, it's probably not accidental that my favorite Mage group is the Hollow Ones (and not because I'm a goth. I'm a geek goth at best, although I like the gothic aesthetics) and not the ones strongly based on real-world organized religions and faiths. So, I could relate to the idea of not liking those. However, I <i>do </i>like the idea of magic, so one could say I'm not as much pro-Traditions/anti-Technocracy, as pro-magick/anti-Technocracy. Although I'm not against technology at all, IMO it could work along magic just fine, given the opportunity and that's why I'm leaning toward the Traditions, if I must to choose between the two, because the Technocracy is forcing one paradigm, just like any organized religion, while the Traditions baseline is that different paradigms could coexist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-30-2017, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T12:50:19-08:00","id":1040822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040808#post1040808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Could the Order of Reason be behind that? Yes, but overall it doesn't fit with their goals as much as conversion does.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there were numerous Mage or Sorcerer groups among the Native Americans (perhaps including Archmages or Oracles that could dwell on Earth due to being anchored in the decidely mystic beliefs of the people), then it makes sense that Order of Reason would kill their people to eliminate them. Not neccesirely because of OoR's outright hostility - perhaps the Native American Mages were the ones who were aggressive? They might have even threatened to attack Europe (with plagues, or curses of unrest, strife, and failed harvests).<br /> Maybe the American Garou were the ones that sparked the hostility between Europeans and Americans? (Though I recall Werewolf has the European Garou as the ones to blame.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:12:12-08:00","id":1040836,"title":"","content":"The Native Americans didn't want the Europeans to invade them, so they resisted. I think I would have resisted if people invaded my homeland, stole my land, and enslaved my people. The Spanish nearly annihilated the Caribbean Native American population through a combination of slavery and disease and, before the establishment of the trans-Atlantic slave trade, North American Native Americans were enslaved by European slavers and sold to be worked to death on the Spanish sugar plantations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:58:22-08:00","id":1040876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040782#post1040782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most likely the Void Engineers by the way of the NWO, since exploration is their thing. Also the Syndicate since colonization was seen as an economic thing for Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Age of Exploration was around the mid-16th Century. Neither the NWO, the Syndicate nor the Void Engineers existed back then.<br /> <br /> The closest you would have had would be the High Guild who managed Commerce, and the Void Seekers, who managed Geography. They would have been the ones who'd start the colonies.<br /> <br /> There was nothing remotely similar to NWO back then though and they barely resemble Their predecessors, the Cabal of Pure Thought, who were deeply devout Catholics with little tolerance for any wayward souls, they even used to aligned with what is now called the Celestial Chorus. By this point in the history, they weren't even an official part of the Order of Reason, but imposed their presence onto them to keep an eye on them, convert them to God from within, and leech of their produce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:04:15-08:00","id":1040877,"title":"","content":"There are two things to remember. First, not every human evil is the fault of the Technocracy and the OoR - mortal man is more than capable of orchestrating atrocities on his own, and when we don't have strong evidence, it's a bit glib to go 'by the way the technocracy = the native american genocide'. Second, the Native American dreamspeakers did more than just resist an invasion. They joined the Traditions before any major contact between Europe and the Americas (not including the Norse settlements), as did the Mayan Euthanatoi, which means that when the Order <i>did</i> arrive in America in any numbers, they had already been fighting native American magi in Europe for some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T17:14:21-08:00","id":1040978,"title":"","content":"A big portion of the exploration fo the new world, like in Mexico and South America, was done by Cainites. Cortes was a pawn of Helena, who was searching for Menele on the other side of the ocean, Most of Cortes men on the other side were Sabbat, and they warred against the Methuselahs who controlled the Aztech empire.<br /> <br /> I think Technocracy was more active later, at the time of the indian wars.<br /> <br /> And I would not exclude the presence of Choristers among the gesuits in South America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 01-30-2017, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T17:59:43-08:00","id":1041001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040820#post1040820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agree and I might add that they're just less apparent and active on the forums.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> People always say that, but I don't know. Ok, I read the NWO one and parts of the VE one. The NWO one, I found them after that no better, on the contrary. Probably it played into it, that I read it as someone who didn't like the Union from the get-go, but the book didn't convinced me to change my opinion. I'm honestly curious how many anti-Technocracy players thought after those books that they're in fact sympathetic. I somewhat suspect it's more like the Hollow Ones book, if you liked the concept, but had problems with the implementation, the books might succeed to shed a new, more nuanced light into it and thus making them better, but if you didn't like the concept at all, then the books won't change that. But it's an interesting topic, it would be good to hear other people's different experiences.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I suspect that this is the biggest part and it connects to the prevalence on forums. Most people on the forums are probably science and technology-minded people, with strong feelings toward modern concepts (dare I say, &amp;quot;The Amercian Way&amp;quot;? I don't mean it as a snide, but it has positive and negative implications) and the Technocracy could represent that. However:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't like organized religion either. Never did, never will. I'm not a religious person at all. But I never saw the traditions just as organized religions, at least not the entirety of it. However, it's probably not accidental that my favorite Mage group is the Hollow Ones (and not because I'm a goth. I'm a geek goth at best, although I like the gothic aesthetics) and not the ones strongly based on real-world organized religions and faiths. So, I could relate to the idea of not liking those. However, I <i>do </i>like the idea of magic, so one could say I'm not as much pro-Traditions/anti-Technocracy, as pro-magick/anti-Technocracy. Although I'm not against technology at all, IMO it could work along magic just fine, given the opportunity and that's why I'm leaning toward the Traditions, if I must to choose between the two, because the Technocracy is forcing one paradigm, just like any organized religion, while the Traditions baseline is that different paradigms could coexist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the traditions would be killing each other and WILL kill each other without the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> In fact, the only reason for the existence of the Traditions is to opose the Union.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:02:17-08:00","id":1041004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040822#post1040822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there were numerous Mage or Sorcerer groups among the Native Americans (perhaps including Archmages or Oracles that could dwell on Earth due to being anchored in the decidely mystic beliefs of the people), then it makes sense that Order of Reason would kill their people to eliminate them. Not neccesirely because of OoR's outright hostility - perhaps the Native American Mages were the ones who were aggressive? They might have even threatened to attack Europe (with plagues, or curses of unrest, strife, and failed harvests).<br /> Maybe the American Garou were the ones that sparked the hostility between Europeans and Americans? (Though I recall Werewolf has the European Garou as the ones to blame.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sifilis were a terrible disease in Europe. Europe suffered under many plagues of S\u00edfilis, Napoles in Italy were almost whiped out by it.<br /> <br /> And s\u00edfilis is a disease that came from the Americas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:13:14-08:00","id":1041014,"title":"","content":"The only reason for the <i>Council</i> is to oppose the Union, though even that isn't quite true. Each of the Traditions has its own purpose, extending well beyond 'oppose the Union'. Take the Order of Hermes. If it's sole purpose for existence is to oppose the Union, then it formed some 600 years too early. That's because it's actual purpose is the advancement of the magus in knowledge and the refinement of the hermetic science, and ultimately, to know the name of God/the Unity/etc by comprehension of the Mysteries. The Verbena's purpose is to maintain the ancient customs, to honour their ancestors and the spiritual entities they enter into compacts with, and to see that the wheel of seasons turns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:14:52-08:00","id":1041015,"title":"","content":"Well, the Council of Nine arose in 1466 to oppose the Order of Reason. The Technocratic Union did not arise from the Order of Reason until 1851, during the Reorganization, after three of its Conventions were destroyed or disbanded (the Solificati, the Craftmasons, and the Order of Pure Thought). In many ways, the Technocratic Union was created from the worst parts of the Order of Reason, and it was founded by European Mages for the benefit of European Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:16:19-08:00","id":1041018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040836#post1040836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Native Americans didn't want the Europeans to invade them, so they resisted. I think I would have resisted if people invaded my homeland, stole my land, and enslaved my people. The Spanish nearly annihilated the Caribbean Native American population through a combination of slavery and disease and, before the establishment of the trans-Atlantic slave trade, North American Native Americans were enslaved by European slavers and sold to be worked to death on the Spanish sugar plantations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The natives were pretty good at genocide and slavery themselves. When the europeans reached the Americas, they had already extincted MANY ethinical groups that lived here before the Europeans.<br /> <br /> Besides, most of the times, the natives wanted to USE the europeans in THEIR wars. Here in South America, for example, documents from the portuguese crown show an interesting situation; the portuguese were allies to the Tupinamb\u00e1s, and enemies to the Tupiniquins, who were allies to the French.<br /> <br /> Thing is, in the last five centuries, the Tupiniquins were advancing South, pushing the lands of the Tupinamb\u00e1s more and more to the South, on many extermination wars. They were hateful enemies.<br /> <br /> In one ocasion, the Tupiniquins went on a disagreement with the portuguese and broke the alliance.<br /> <br /> What put the portuguese in awe... Is that after that, the Tupinamb\u00e1s, who had been ALWAYS hostile to them, came to offer them their alliance.<br /> <br /> The natives hated each others. In North America, they would change fur to the colonials for guns and horses... And would use those against each other even more than against &quot;the evil white men&quot;.<br /> <br /> The myth of &quot;the noble savage&quot; is just that: a myth. And a childish myth, used only to demonize the western civilization (the place of that demonic thing called &quot;capitalism&quot;, the big Satan).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:19:06-08:00","id":1041019,"title":"","content":"Omg, you guys are really annoying on the details... You know what I mean. The only reason those guys are losely toghether is to fight the Union... Or if you prefer, the OoR (oh, the details). Comon, you understood what I was trying to say","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:19:43-08:00","id":1041021,"title":"","content":"Surprisingly, it is possible for both sides to do terrible things, but for one side to still be worse. Morality is not a zero sum game, and neither is history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:24:18-08:00","id":1041026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041001#post1041001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except the traditions would be killing each other and WILL kill each other without the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> In fact, the only reason for the existence of the Traditions is to opose the Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second part is not true, just the others said. My apologies, but you seem to have a very lopsided view of the traditions.<br /> <br /> Besides, the Union in turn wouldn't exist without the Order of Hermes. We could do this all day.<br /> <br /> Without the Union, oh sure, there would be confrontations between fractions. That's human nature. That doesn't mean they wouldn't be able to coexist. Sure, an outward threat does a lot to minimize those conflicts, that's again, human nature. However, we aren't living in the dark ages anymore. Most members of the traditions are grown up in the modern world, they probably wouldn't go to full-on war without a very good reason, like the threat of extinction.<br /> <br /> We have conflicts in the real world between philosophies and religions and there are fanatics, yes, but still, we manage to coexist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-30-2017, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:30:13-08:00","id":1041029,"title":"","content":"The Noble Savage is an archetype that was created during the 17th century to describe the futility of the fight of the Native Americans against the Europeans (the first use of the term in English was by John Dryden in 1672). Whatever the Native Americans did to themselves, it was the Europeans who brought the diseases that killed countless millions, it was the Europeans who bought the Native American slaves and sent them by the countless millions to die from overwork and starvation in the sugar plantations of the Caribbean, and it was the Europeans who killed off most of the remaining Native Americans and stole their land. It is historically inaccurate to claim that the Europeans did not commit genocide, especially it was the stated policy of many of the Europeans powers at the time to take the land of the Native Americans for themselves and to kill off any Native Americans who resisted (a policy that was continued in the United States and Canada up until the 1960s with the policy of 'Kill the Indian, Save the Man' that typified the Native American Residential Schools). The United States and Canada also violated countless treaties with the Native Americans because no one with power cared about the rights of the Native Americans until after World War Two (just like no one with power really cared about segregation and the civil rights abuses against African Americans or Hispanic Americans until after World War Two).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:32:05-08:00","id":1041030,"title":"","content":"For a particularly good example, the Order of Hermes not only can, but has, coexist with the other Traditions and their antecedents for a long time. There's the odd bit of tension with various groups over nodes, but there are no major ideological bars to a Hermetic and a Verbena sitting down to lunch even without the Council of Nine (and when we recall that House Diedne and House Bjornaer existed and had more to do with the Verbena than with the stereotype of the Hermetic; that the Batini and the Shaea have much in common; that the Sons of Ether outright come from Hermetic roots...), nor to most of the traditions doing the same. The sole exception tends to be the Chorus, and even that only in its more radical, zealous form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:32:58-08:00","id":1041031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041021#post1041021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surprisingly, it is possible for both sides to do terrible things, but for one side to still be worse. Morality is not a zero sum game, and neither is history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree. The Europeans did terrible things. The Natives did terrible things. The Americas weren't a peaceful paradise before the Europeans, but the Europeans weren't innocent bystanders by a long shot. In the end and on the long run, they managed to take over, so the Natives were the losing side and they lost badly. That native tribes and empires killed each other to extinction before that doesn't redeem the terrible things the Europeans did to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:37:00-08:00","id":1041033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041029#post1041029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Noble Savage is an archetype that was created during the 17th century to describe the futility of the fight of the Native Americans against the Europeans (the first use of the term in English was by John Dryden in 1672). Whatever the Native Americans did to themselves, it was the Europeans who brought the diseases that killed countless millions, it was the Europeans who bought the Native American slaves and sent them by the countless millions to die from overwork and starvation in the sugar plantations of the Caribbean, and it was the Europeans who killed off most of the remaining Native Americans and stole their land. It is historically inaccurate to claim that the Europeans did not commit genocide, especially it was the stated policy of many of the Europeans powers at the time to take the land of the Native Americans for themselves and to kill off any Native Americans who resisted (a policy that was continued in the United States and Canada up until the 1960s with the policy of 'Kill the Indian, Save the Man' that typified the Native American Residential Schools). The United States and Canada also violated countless treaties with the Native Americans because no one with power cared about the rights of the Native Americans until after World War Two (just like no one with power really cared about segregation and the civil rights abuses against African Americans or Hispanic Americans until after World War Two).</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically it's the same problem, when people start throwing numbers of how much more people the Stalinism killed than the Nazis. Like that fact would redeem the Nazis in any way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:37:48-08:00","id":1041034,"title":"","content":"The Council of Nine is an alloy, like bronze, and it is stronger and tougher than its components. The Technocracy is a pure metal, like iron, and it is soft and brittle and, because it is soft and brittle, it is incapable of tolerating any dissent because it would fall apart if any understood its weaknesses. The Order of Reason was steel until it destroyed the Craftmasons because the Craftmasons cared about the Masses, something that is missing in the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:41:51-08:00","id":1041038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041026#post1041026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The second part is not true, just the others said. My apologies, but you seem to have a very lopsided view of the traditions.<br /> <br /> Besides, the Union in turn wouldn't exist without the Order of Hermes. We could do this all day.<br /> <br /> Without the Union, oh sure, there would be confrontations between fractions. That's human nature. That doesn't mean they wouldn't be able to coexist. Sure, an outward threat does a lot to minimize those conflicts, that's again, human nature. However, we aren't living in the dark ages anymore. Most members of the traditions are grown up in the modern world, they probably wouldn't go to full-on war without a very good reason, like the threat of extinction.<br /> <br /> We have conflicts in the real world between philosophies and religions and there are fanatics, yes, but still, we manage to coexist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you can thank the atomic bombs for that. Without the power of the atom, we probably would be fighting World War 4 by now, because there is no doubt that EUA+Europe would had gone on a full out war against USSR+China<br /> <br /> Also, all those ideas of &quot;tolerance&quot; only came after the horrors of WWII that completely shocked the world.<br /> <br /> By evolution, we were made to be xenophobics. In our evolutionary history, humans developed empathy towards those of the same tribe/group/clan/etc. Our empathy allows us to work in group, which increases the chances of survival to all.<br /> <br /> However, the aliens, those outside the group, others... They were competition. The other tribe would kill you for your food. They would kill you for your women. And they would kill you for your cozy cave.<br /> <br /> Not hating outsiders meant death. So, evolution selected the most xenophobics amongst our ancestors; those with more distrust towards outsiders lived, those that shared empathy to humans outside the group, died.<br /> <br /> And that's not human nature, it's just nature. Cruel, merciless, and completely oblivious to our existence. The worse enemy of a Lion is another of it's kind. And that holds true for any organism in this planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:50:27-08:00","id":1041040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041030#post1041030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a particularly good example, the Order of Hermes not only can, but has, coexist with the other Traditions and their antecedents for a long time. There's the odd bit of tension with various groups over nodes, but there are no major ideological bars to a Hermetic and a Verbena sitting down to lunch even without the Council of Nine (and when we recall that House Diedne and House Bjornaer existed and had more to do with the Verbena than with the stereotype of the Hermetic; that the Batini and the Shaea have much in common; that the Sons of Ether outright come from Hermetic roots...), nor to most of the traditions doing the same. The sole exception tends to be the Chorus, and even that only in its more radical, zealous form.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Order of Hermes were as powerful and diverse as both the Order of Reason and the Traditions at their time, considering the scales of time. They are my favorite along the Traditions alongside the Sons of Ether (for different reasons). Besides, they too were a meritocratic society, which tends to take away many prejudices. But they are an exception rather than the rule.<br /> <br /> What has always truly puzzled me is why haven't the Hermetics joined the OoR en masse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:54:01-08:00","id":1041041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041038#post1041038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, you can thank the atomic bombs for that. Without the power of the atom, we probably would be fighting World War 4 by now, because there is no doubt that EUA+Europe would had gone on a full out war against USSR+China<br /> <br /> Also, all those ideas of &quot;tolerance&quot; only came after the horrors of WWII that completely shocked the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> All hail The Atomic Bomb, our righteous, noble and benevolent savior!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By evolution, we were made to be xenophobics. In our evolutionary history, humans developed empathy towards those of the same tribe/group/clan/etc. Our empathy allows us to work in group, which increases the chances of survival to all.<br /> <br /> However, the aliens, those outside the group, others... They were competition. The other tribe would kill you for your food. They would kill you for your women. And they would kill you for your cozy cave.<br /> <br /> Not hating outsiders meant death. So, evolution selected the most xenophobics amongst our ancestors; those with more distrust towards outsiders lived, those that shared empathy to humans outside the group, died.<br /> <br /> And that's not human nature, it's just nature. Cruel, merciless, and completely oblivious to our existence. The worse enemy of a Lion is another of it's kind. And that holds true for any organism in this planet. </div> </div> </div>One, tribalism is indeed an evolutionary mechanism. Two, that didn't stop people to forge bigger covenants all through history. Things happened between the neolithic and WW2 you know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:55:37-08:00","id":1041043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041040#post1041040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What has always truly puzzled me is why haven't the Hermetics joined the OoR en masse</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm, because the OoR blown up one of their biggest strongholds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:55:58-08:00","id":1041044,"title":"","content":"Nope, the idea that xenophobia is part of human biology is contrary to everything we know about anthropology, and I think that you are confusing human social evolution for human biological evolution (humans have not changed that much biologically over the last 500,000 years, but we have change socially many, many times during that time period). There is very little evidence of violence between hominids in the skeletons that we have found and ritual cannibalism within the same tribal group was actually more common that tribal warfare for most of human existence. In fact, most tribal groups seemed to have practiced reproductive outcrossing with their neighbors (anthropologists find little evidence of inbreeding before Neolithic times), which makes sense if you do not want to be constantly worrying about your neighbors killing you in your sleep and taking your women because your neighbors are either your brothers or your women are their sisters. It was not until you got to the Neolithic era that you started to see evidence of widespread violence between groups, probably due to the social (not biological) evolution of xenophobia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:58:02-08:00","id":1041045,"title":"","content":"Dear Journal.<br /> <br /> We're 12 pages in and there's no sign of a cease fire.<br /> <br /> Diplomacy has failed, Communications are tense, and appeals of &quot;Guys! You're both right!&quot; have fallen to these steadfast legions.<br /> <br /> On one side, the Anti-crats. Adamant in their assertions that Tech is only a solution for the destruction tech has brought upon the earth.<br /> While opposing them, are the Techno-pros, Unwilling to shift their claim that without Tech there would be no progress, and only stagnation.<br /> <br /> It's hard to think back, all those....4 days ago, how did this all begin? A simple comment, an expression of an opinion. an exchange of conflicting views... Then came the Anthropologists and the Historians, experts in their fields, willing to use real world claims to back up their notes. Then the Canon's were brought out, each one firing an impressive display of completely made up but generally accepted an adhered to facts. The carnage was brutal on all sides was brutal.<br /> Throughout the flurry of History lessons and Source book references, a number of voices were heard, appeals to emotion. Cries for the glory that is tech, anger towards the evil that is control. All of which built up a great catalogue of interpretive thoughts.<br /> <br /> We are all experts. We are all essayists. We are all the masters of our own downfall. Don't you see? We brought this upon ourselves. For each one feels entitled to their own interpretation, but to justify their own convictions, they must destroy any attempt to undermine our own theories. Our own theories about a world which we created, and we have the power to change because it doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> The facts are not facts. The History is optional. The main events are modular. And the masterminds are whatever makes sense at the time. Such ideas cannot be tolerated by either side. There is only one way to interpret this game, only one! Perhaps the only thing either end may agree on is that only one view can stand...<br /> <br /> We are trapped in a bitter war that has no end, no real purpose. As discussion continues to deteriorate, the massive walls of impenetrable explanation are being built, and cries of &quot;Do what you're like, but this is why you're wrong&quot; echo in all directions.<br /> <br /> What is there left to blame? Will an agreement ever be met? If neither side will back down I can only see one logical endpoint.<br /> <br /> Calling each other stupid.<br /> <br /> I pray it will not come to this.<br /> <br /> Signed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T19:02:11-08:00","id":1041047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041031#post1041031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agree. The Europeans did terrible things. The Natives did terrible things. The Americas weren't a peaceful paradise before the Europeans, but the Europeans weren't innocent bystanders by a long shot. In the end and on the long run, they managed to take over, so the Natives were the losing side and they lost badly. That native tribes and empires killed each other to extinction before that doesn't redeem the terrible things the Europeans did to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is innocent in history. Trying to villanize or make heroes from the losing side is a poor reductionism.<br /> <br /> Muslims genocided 80 millions of hindus at India. They are responsible for at least 112 millions of slaves throughout their 14 centuries of history. They commited extensive bloody genocides on Europe, Asia and Africa. They've wiped out many cultures in their way.<br /> <br /> Many African kingdoms had economies who were absolutely dependant on slavery. Big, adavnced and powerful kingdoms, like the kingdom of Mali. At the beggining of the Age of Discovery, the europeans weren't using slaves; the system in Europe were of servitute. It were the africans that made the europeans &quot;remember&quot; how to use slaves.<br /> <br /> And the mongolians were amonsgt the most brutal conquerors ever, and spawned a huge empire over Asia and Europe.<br /> <br /> Should we call the mongolians, now an insignificant and nomadic people, accountable for all the barbaric atrocities of their ancestors? Should we consider the modern muslims the evil encarnated because of the bloody history of islam? Should we blame the poor countries on Africa as inhuman exploiters slavers?<br /> <br /> That kind of superficial judgment of the western civilization is a shallow line of thought","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T19:07:12-08:00","id":1041048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041045#post1041045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear Journal.<br /> <br /> We're 12 pages in and there's no sign of a cease fire.<br /> <br /> Diplomacy has failed, Communications are tense, and appeals of &quot;Guys! You're both right!&quot; have fallen to these steadfast legions.<br /> <br /> On one side, the Anti-crats. Adamant in their assertions that Tech is only a solution for the destruction tech has brought upon the earth.<br /> While opposing them, are the Techno-pros, Unwilling to shift their claim that without Tech there would be no progress, and only stagnation.<br /> <br /> It's hard to think back, all those....4 days ago, how did this all begin? A simple comment, an expression of an opinion. an exchange of conflicting views... Then came the Anthropologists and the Historians, experts in their fields, willing to use real world claims to back up their notes. Then the Canon's were brought out, each one firing an impressive display of completely made up but generally accepted an adhered to facts. The carnage was brutal on all sides was brutal.<br /> Throughout the flurry of History lessons and Source book references, a number of voices were heard, appeals to emotion. Cries for the glory that is tech, anger towards the evil that is control. All of which built up a great catalogue of interpretive thoughts.<br /> <br /> We are all experts. We are all essayists. We are all the masters of our own downfall. Don't you see? We brought this upon ourselves. For each one feels entitled to their own interpretation, but to justify their own convictions, they must destroy any attempt to undermine our own theories. Our own theories about a world which we created, and we have the power to change because it doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> The facts are not facts. The History is optional. The main events are modular. And the masterminds are whatever makes sense at the time. Such ideas cannot be tolerated by either side. There is only one way to interpret this game, only one! Perhaps the only thing either end may agree on is that only one view can stand...<br /> <br /> We are trapped in a bitter war that has no end, no real purpose. As discussion continues to deteriorate, the massive walls of impenetrable explanation are being built, and cries of &quot;Do what you're like, but this is why you're wrong&quot; echo in all directions.<br /> <br /> What is there left to blame? Will an agreement ever be met? If neither side will back down I can only see one logical endpoint.<br /> <br /> Calling each other stupid.<br /> <br /> I pray it will not come to this.<br /> <br /> Signed</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.blastwave-comic.com/index.php?p=comic&amp;nro=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.blastwave-comic.com/index.php?p=comic&amp;nro=1\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.blastwave-comic.com/index.php?p=comic&amp;nro=1\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.blastwave-comic.com/index.php?p=comic&amp;nro=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T19:18:26-08:00","id":1041052,"title":"","content":"The violence in the Neolitic is due to the advent of agriculture, which started a technological revolution beyond anything before that allowed humans to reach numbers higher than ever. With the agriculture, war was invented.<br /> <br /> The low signs of violence prior to that is because human groups were too few and too sparced. So, your neighbors in a area of many, many miles, were indeed your brothers and sisters; the first groups, being all nomadic, couldn't hold a lot of individuals, so, after a certain size, the group would have to split.<br /> <br /> And, like I said, humans were empathetic towards each other <i>within the same group </i>. Evolution also created this on us. But we have ALWAYS been xenophobics towards <i>outsiders</i>.<br /> <br /> What does that mean? It means that, in a radius of 100 miles, every little group of a few dozens were &quot;members of the tribe&quot;. But, 200 miles away, there would be &quot;the others&quot; - a different tribe. And those would NEVER cross the territory of the others - because they hated each other.<br /> <br /> Xenophobia is not an exclusively human merit. It's all over the animal kingdom. Territory is one of the most important matters to many species. And the hominids weren't evolving only in the last 500.000 years. All those traits have been shaped since the times of our common ancestry with apes.<br /> <br /> By the way, apes have that same behavioral pattern - empathy in group, xenophobia towards outsiders","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T19:27:20-08:00","id":1041055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041045#post1041045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear Journal.<br /> <br /> We're 12 pages in and there's no sign of a cease fire.<br /> <br /> Diplomacy has failed, Communications are tense, and appeals of &amp;quot;Guys! You're both right!&amp;quot; have fallen to these steadfast legions.<br /> <br /> On one side, the Anti-crats. Adamant in their assertions that Tech is only a solution for the destruction tech has brought upon the earth.<br /> While opposing them, are the Techno-pros, Unwilling to shift their claim that without Tech there would be no progress, and only stagnation.<br /> <br /> It's hard to think back, all those....4 days ago, how did this all begin? A simple comment, an expression of an opinion. an exchange of conflicting views... Then came the Anthropologists and the Historians, experts in their fields, willing to use real world claims to back up their notes. Then the Canon's were brought out, each one firing an impressive display of completely made up but generally accepted an adhered to facts. The carnage was brutal on all sides was brutal.<br /> Throughout the flurry of History lessons and Source book references, a number of voices were heard, appeals to emotion. Cries for the glory that is tech, anger towards the evil that is control. All of which built up a great catalogue of interpretive thoughts.<br /> <br /> We are all experts. We are all essayists. We are all the masters of our own downfall. Don't you see? We brought this upon ourselves. For each one feels entitled to their own interpretation, but to justify their own convictions, they must destroy any attempt to undermine our own theories. Our own theories about a world which we created, and we have the power to change because it doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> The facts are not facts. The History is optional. The main events are modular. And the masterminds are whatever makes sense at the time. Such ideas cannot be tolerated by either side. There is only one way to interpret this game, only one! Perhaps the only thing either end may agree on is that only one view can stand...<br /> <br /> We are trapped in a bitter war that has no end, no real purpose. As discussion continues to deteriorate, the massive walls of impenetrable explanation are being built, and cries of &amp;quot;Do what you're like, but this is why you're wrong&amp;quot; echo in all directions.<br /> <br /> What is there left to blame? Will an agreement ever be met? If neither side will back down I can only see one logical endpoint.<br /> <br /> Calling each other stupid.<br /> <br /> I pray it will not come to this.<br /> <br /> Signed</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I enjoy the intellectual sport. And I don't like discussions were all sides agree on everything... I love the duel of ideas.<br /> <br /> And I also love the way that people truly take sides on an invented, imaginary, non real game. It's like watching the in-game several propagandas clashing in a very real sense. It gives me the real notion of &quot;how would it be&quot;. I think it's enriching for the game experience.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, and long live the imaginary Union, death to the imaginary Traditions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T19:29:57-08:00","id":1041056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041047#post1041047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nobody is innocent in history. Trying to villanize or make heroes from the losing side is a poor reductionism.<br /> <br /> Muslims genocided 80 millions of hindus at India. They are responsible for at least 112 millions of slaves throughout their 14 centuries of history. They commited extensive bloody genocides on Europe, Asia and Africa. They've wiped out many cultures in their way.<br /> <br /> Many African kingdoms had economies who were absolutely dependant on slavery. Big, adavnced and powerful kingdoms, like the kingdom of Mali. At the beggining of the Age of Discovery, the europeans weren't using slaves; the system in Europe were of servitute. It were the africans that made the europeans &quot;remember&quot; how to use slaves.<br /> <br /> And the mongolians were amonsgt the most brutal conquerors ever, and spawned a huge empire over Asia and Europe.<br /> <br /> Should we call the mongolians, now an insignificant and nomadic people, accountable for all the barbaric atrocities of their ancestors? Should we consider the modern muslims the evil encarnated because of the bloody history of islam? Should we blame the poor countries on Africa as inhuman exploiters slavers?<br /> <br /> That kind of superficial judgment of the western civilization is a shallow line of thought</div> </div> </div> </div>You mistake '15th, 16th, 17th, etc century europeans were dickheads to native peoples in America' for a condemnation of modern Western civilization. It isn't, so you're arguing against a point that no one is seriously making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T19:30:37-08:00","id":1041057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041045#post1041045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear Journal.<br /> <br /> We're 12 pages in and there's no sign of a cease fire.<br /> <br /> Diplomacy has failed, Communications are tense, and appeals of &quot;Guys! You're both right!&quot; have fallen to these steadfast legions.<br /> <br /> On one side, the Anti-crats. Adamant in their assertions that Tech is only a solution for the destruction tech has brought upon the earth.<br /> While opposing them, are the Techno-pros, Unwilling to shift their claim that without Tech there would be no progress, and only stagnation.<br /> <br /> It's hard to think back, all those....4 days ago, how did this all begin? A simple comment, an expression of an opinion. an exchange of conflicting views... Then came the Anthropologists and the Historians, experts in their fields, willing to use real world claims to back up their notes. Then the Canon's were brought out, each one firing an impressive display of completely made up but generally accepted an adhered to facts. The carnage was brutal on all sides was brutal.<br /> Throughout the flurry of History lessons and Source book references, a number of voices were heard, appeals to emotion. Cries for the glory that is tech, anger towards the evil that is control. All of which built up a great catalogue of interpretive thoughts.<br /> <br /> We are all experts. We are all essayists. We are all the masters of our own downfall. Don't you see? We brought this upon ourselves. For each one feels entitled to their own interpretation, but to justify their own convictions, they must destroy any attempt to undermine our own theories. Our own theories about a world which we created, and we have the power to change because it doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> The facts are not facts. The History is optional. The main events are modular. And the masterminds are whatever makes sense at the time. Such ideas cannot be tolerated by either side. There is only one way to interpret this game, only one! Perhaps the only thing either end may agree on is that only one view can stand...<br /> <br /> We are trapped in a bitter war that has no end, no real purpose. As discussion continues to deteriorate, the massive walls of impenetrable explanation are being built, and cries of &quot;Do what you're like, but this is why you're wrong&quot; echo in all directions.<br /> <br /> What is there left to blame? Will an agreement ever be met? If neither side will back down I can only see one logical endpoint.<br /> <br /> Calling each other stupid.<br /> <br /> I pray it will not come to this.<br /> <br /> Signed</div> </div> </div> </div>No YOU'RE STUPID!<br /> <br /> (<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T19:32:45-08:00","id":1041058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041057#post1041057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No YOU'RE STUPID!<br /> <br /> (<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</div> </div> </div> </div>My God...<br /> <br /> It is already too late!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T19:53:37-08:00","id":1041065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041056#post1041056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mistake '15th, 16th, 17th, etc century europeans were dickheads to native peoples in America' for a condemnation of modern Western civilization. It isn't, so you're arguing against a point that no one is seriously making.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, there are certain similarities between Aya's arguments and arguments to be had frequently elsewhere. Given that online debate forums tend to engender something akin to muscle memory, only for arguments, I can see how certain things can come up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T21:58:52-08:00","id":1041104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040468#post1040468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure? The most powerful force for oppressive, brutish and controlling organized religion was not the Celestial Chorus, but the Cabal of Pure Thought and the Messianic Voices, who split into the CPT and the Chouer Celeste in due time.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about fictitious mystical orders like the celestial chorus, I'm talking about real world religious groups, especially those who tried to control societies by controlling what people believed.<br /> <br /> When you look at the sort of power and freedom that technology has given people and compare that to what people had a 1,000 years ago, it becomes easy to support the technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T22:14:09-08:00","id":1041106,"title":"","content":"You do not need religion to have oppression, look at Hitler, Stalin, and Mao.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T22:15:51-08:00","id":1041107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041104#post1041104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not talking about fictitious mystical orders like the celestial chorus, I'm talking about real world religious groups, especially those who tried to control societies by controlling what people believed.<br /> <br /> When you look at the sort of power and freedom that technology has given people and compare that to what people had a 1,000 years ago, it becomes easy to support the technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, though. The OoR and the Technocracy are, at least in Mage, major factors behind those real world religious groups trying to control societies by controlling what the people believe. That was literally the Cabal of Pure Thought's goal, just as it is the NWO's after (and yes, the NWO still has ties to religion in the modern WoD), so it's not as straightforward as 'technology sets us free from the shackles of religion, therefore technocrats = good' because the technocrats and their forebears <i>imposed</i> many of those shackles in the first place.<br /> <br /> You can't divorce the one from the other, and that's the whole point of the Technocracy - it's meant to have both positive and negative aspects, to be a thing of glorious hope and beauty that (just like real-life technocratic and futurist philosophies have had an unfortunate tendency to do) followed its ideology down some tricky corners to a place of brutal fascism and oppression. To just go 'technology good, religion bad, therefore technocrats good' misses by a wide mile.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T22:17:21-08:00","id":1041108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041106#post1041106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do not need religion to have oppression, look at Hitler, Stalin, and Mao.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am well aware of that fact and was aware of it well before your reminded me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T00:49:39-08:00","id":1041143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041107#post1041107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the thing, though. The OoR and the Technocracy are, at least in Mage, major factors behind those real world religious groups trying to control societies by controlling what the people believe. That was literally the Cabal of Pure Thought's goal, just as it is the NWO's after (and yes, the NWO still has ties to religion in the modern WoD), so it's not as straightforward as 'technology sets us free from the shackles of religion, therefore technocrats = good' because the technocrats and their forebears <i>imposed</i> many of those shackles in the first place.<br /> <br /> You can't divorce the one from the other, and that's the whole point of the Technocracy - it's meant to have both positive and negative aspects, to be a thing of glorious hope and beauty that (just like real-life technocratic and futurist philosophies have had an unfortunate tendency to do) followed its ideology down some tricky corners to a place of brutal fascism and oppression. To just go 'technology good, religion bad, therefore technocrats good' misses by a wide mile.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think my statement is done justice by your summary of thoughts then you have totally misunderstood me by assuming a false conclusion.<br /> <br /> I do not feel that the Technocracy is devoid of past involvement with religion(s) through the Order of Reason, nor do I feel that it does not have a (less powerful) connection to religion(s) today.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, I have never divorced religion from the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> You have assumed this without any legitimate reason.<br /> <br /> My previoous statements however may have led you to this conclusion so I don't blame you for misreading my words. I was merely trying to explain the reason why many people, other people in fact, seem to love the technocracy so much. That is, after all, what the original post was all about in part.<br /> <br /> Many people on this forum have often ignored the history of Mage and so they should, many of them don't have time to read tomes of fictional history, particularly if they will never play anything resembling a historical game.<br /> <br /> Since they don't know of the long history of Christian supremacy within the Order of Reason (particularly the uniquely patriarchal, deistic and rationalist Christianity which the Order embraced) they don't know that religion was a big part of the Technocracy and don't really see it, to them, the Ascension War is a fight between two factions, one of which (we know falsely) represents 'freedom' from religion and the other represents the 'old ways' (which we know is not another way of saying religion).<br /> <br /> I was merely explaining ONE reason why the Union is so popular.<br /> <br /> And I never even got into outright technophilia AKA how massive transforming mechs and cyborgs with laser rifles popping out of their backs makes some people turned on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T02:41:17-08:00","id":1041158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041143#post1041143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you think my statement is done justice by your summary of thoughts then you have totally misunderstood me by assuming a false conclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not feel that the Technocracy is devoid of past involvement with religion(s) through the Order of Reason, nor do I feel that it does not have a (less powerful) connection to religion(s) today.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, I have never divorced religion from the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> You have assumed this without any legitimate reason. </div> </div> </div>I have assumed this because you have posted, repeatedly, that 'technology good, religion bad, therefore technocracy good'. I think that reason is legitimate in its own right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My previoous statements however may have led you to this conclusion so I don't blame you for misreading my words. I was merely trying to explain the reason why many people, other people in fact, seem to love the technocracy so much. That is, after all, what the original post was all about in part. </div> </div> </div>And yet, your prior statements have all been expressed as personal statements in pretty much every respect. So either I'm very badly misreading your words, or you're very badly failing to communicate your actual points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Many people on this forum have often ignored the history of Mage and so they should, many of them don't have time to read tomes of fictional history, particularly if they will never play anything resembling a historical game.<br /> <br /> Since they don't know of the long history of Christian supremacy within the Order of Reason (particularly the uniquely patriarchal, deistic and rationalist Christianity which the Order embraced) they don't know that religion was a big part of the Technocracy and don't really see it, to them, the Ascension War is a fight between two factions, one of which (we know falsely) represents 'freedom' from religion and the other represents the 'old ways' (which we know is not another way of saying religion).<br /> <br /> I was merely explaining ONE reason why the Union is so popular. </div> </div> </div>That may be so, but again, you gave it as <i>your</i> reason for favouring the Technocracy. It's funny that now, you have decided it was never that, just 'what people, y'know, think' to sum up your argument, while previously you have been quite personal in the reasoning. Were you yourself aware of the history of mage in the area?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T03:50:24-08:00","id":1041179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041158#post1041158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have assumed this because you have posted, repeatedly, that 'technology good, religion bad, therefore technocracy good'. I think that reason is legitimate in its own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I haven't, please see my original post, it should be on page ten of this thread In it, I specifically refered to other people and their opinions regarding religion and technology. I did say it becomes easy to support the technocracy but that is not saying &quot;technology good, religion bad&quot;.<br /> <br /> It may be unintentional on your part but you are totally mischaracterizing my words loomer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041158#post1041158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, your prior statements have all been expressed as personal statements in pretty much every respect. So either I'm very badly misreading your words, or you're very badly failing to communicate your actual points.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You have misread me quite badly, as I said above, my original statement referred other peoples opinions explicitly. I was actually trying to explain why other people like the union, I did not express my own feelings about the Union in my original post at all except to say &quot;I love the freedom and power that technology has given me, I don't like the way most organized religions use to control society (and still do to a lesser extent) so I am, like it or not, a technocracy sympathizer. But I still like the traditions better &quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041158#post1041158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That may be so, but again, you gave it as <i>your</i> reason for favouring the Technocracy. It's funny that now, you have decided it was never that, just 'what people, y'know, think' to sum up your argument, while previously you have been quite personal in the reasoning. Were you yourself aware of the history of mage in the area?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You have completely misunderstood me and much of what I've been saying, I don't want to be rude when I tell you that you have gone into total supposition with this last remark. I have a very strong grasp of the history of Mage the Ascension, from the formation of the Ahli Batin on the night of Fana in 509 BC to the formation of the Order of Hermes in 767 AD after Trainoma and Bonisagus helped gather the 12 Magi of the Order to the history of the Cabal of Pure thought and their eventual transformation into the Templars after they were expelled from the Union during it's 19th century purges.<br /> <br /> I admit my words may have misled you but you have also misunderstood me due to your own inaccurate assumptions about what I said.<br /> <br /> I hope this clears things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","user":"Zennis","date":".  Edited for a spelling error 01-31-2017, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T04:16:45-08:00","id":1041186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041179#post1041179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No I haven't, please see my original post, it should be on page ten of this thread In it, I specifically refered to other people and their opinions regarding religion and technology. I did say it becomes easy to support the technocracy but that is not saying &quot;technology good, religion bad&quot;.<br /> <br /> It may be unintentional on your part but you are totally mischaracterizing my words loomer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I quote your initial post in its entirety.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1040463#post1040463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's probably more fans of the traditions out there than there are fans of the union, they may just not be speaking out so much lately.<br /> <br /> Remember that the new convention books coming out and depicting the technocracy in a new way won the technocracy a lot of fans, I too found myself having a new appreciation for it after reading the new books.<br /> <br /> The new books really boosted the fan base but aside from that, there's an underlying reason why a lot of people like the union, they use technology in their daily lives and aren't too hot on organized religion, the tradions have a big tie to organized religions and the union has an even bigger tie to technology, this makes a lot of people inherently biased towards liking the union and this is just one aspect of the tip of the iceberg.<br /> <br /> I love the freedom and power that technology has given me, I don't like the way most organized religions use to control society (and still do to a lesser extent) so I am, like it or not, a technocracy sympathizer.<br /> <br /> But I still like the traditions better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You speak, very strongly, that you <i>personally</i> sympathize on the grounds that 'technology good, religion bad'.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You have misread me quite badly, as I said above, my original statement referred other peoples opinions explicitly. I was actually trying to explain why other people like the union, I did not express my own feelings about the Union in my original post at all except to say &quot;I love the freedom and power that technology has given me, I don't like the way most organized religions use to control society (and still do to a lesser extent) so I am, like it or not, a technocracy sympathizer. But I still like the traditions better &quot; </div> </div> </div>Your first post is quoted in its entirety above. As you note, you have yourself stated your sympathies rest on those grounds, and it is those grounds I am questioning.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You have completely misunderstood me and much of what I've been saying, I don't want to be rude when I tell you that you have gone into total supposition with this last remark. I have a very strong grasp of the history of Mage the Ascension, from the formation of the Ahli Batin on the night of Fana in 509 BC to the formation of the Order of Hermes in 767 AD after Trainoma and Bonisagus helped gather the 12 Magi of the Order to the history of the Cabal of Pure thought and their eventual transformation into the Templars after they were expelled from the Union during it's 19th century purges.<br /> <br /> I admit my words may have misled you but you have also misunderstood me due to your own inaccurate assumptions about what I said.<br /> <br /> I hope this clears things up. </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is supposition, and it was intended to clarify whether or not you fell into the category you nominated. Certainly, your sympathies resting on - again, 'technology good, religion bad' while ignoring the Technocracy's role in the bad elements of religion seemed to suggest it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T04:37:36-08:00","id":1041193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041186#post1041186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You speak, very strongly, that you <i>personally</i> sympathize on the grounds that 'technology good, religion bad'.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No I do not, you do not understand the true sentiment behind my words, you are jumping to false conclusions based on speculation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041186#post1041186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it is supposition, and it was intended to clarify whether or not you fell into the category you nominated. Certainly, your sympathies resting on - again, 'technology good, religion bad' while ignoring the Technocracy's role in the bad elements of religion seemed to suggest it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have never ignored the Union's past in anything, let alone the bad elements of religion, I have never ignored anything in fact, that is entirely speculation on your part. I just didn't bring them up in my post, just like I didn't bring up the Union's role in the holocaust (supporting Nazi Germany so as to bring the world under one government).<br /> <br /> Your speculation that because I didn't bring up the Union's role with regards to religion is no more rational than speculation that I ignore the Union's role in the holocaust.<br /> <br /> Loomer, you've completely misunderstood me, you're making false accusations and coming up with points that have no relation to the reality of my personal views, I respect your attempt at deducing my personal views based on what I said and didn't say earlier in the thread but (and I say with no ill will towards you) you have totally misunderstood me.<br /> <br /> Had you asked me &quot;Zennis, how do you feel about the Union's past regarding religion, particularly Christianity&quot; rather than accused me of harbouring false sentiment, you would have found I do not hold the views which you are attributing to me much sooner than you have now.<br /> <br /> If you wish to continue to mischaracterize my words on this forum then I won't stop you but I will ask you to politely inquire as to my opinions instead.<br /> <br /> I am sure you will find my opinions to be far less one dimensional than you thought previously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T04:49:22-08:00","id":1041196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041193#post1041193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No I do not, you do not understand the true sentiment behind my words, you are jumping to false conclusions based on speculation.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet it is what you said. Or did you not write &quot;I love the freedom and power that technology has given me, I don't like the way most organized religions use to control society (and still do to a lesser extent) so I am, like it or not, a technocracy sympathizer.&quot;? 'Technology good, religion bad, therefore Technocracy good' is a glib summation, I admit, but it is nonetheless accurate your statement. It was a personal statement, it identifies your grounds for sympathy, and it is very clear what you meant despite your protests.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have never ignored the Union's past in anything, let alone the bad elements of religion, I have never ignored anything in fact, that is entirely speculation on your part. I just didn't bring them up in my post, just like I didn't bring up the Union's role in the holocaust (supporting Nazi Germany so as to bring the world under one government).<br /> <br /> Your speculation that because I didn't bring up the Union's role with regards to religion is no more rational than speculation that I ignore the Union's role in the holocaust. </div> </div> </div>Actually, considering that your grounds for sympathy include that you dislike organized religion's attempts to control society, it is quite rational to raise the point that the OoR is an influencing factor in those attempts - and quite rational to assume you either ignore or are unaware of the OoR's history in that area.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Loomer, you've completely misunderstood me, you're making false accusations and coming up with points that have no relation to the reality of my personal views, I respect your attempt at deducing my personal views based on what I said and didn't say earlier in the thread but (and I say with no ill will towards you) you have totally misunderstood me.<br /> <br /> Had you asked me &quot;Zennis, how do you feel about the Union's past regarding religion, particularly Christianity&quot; rather than accused me of harbouring false sentiment, you would have found I do not hold the views which you are attributing to me much sooner than you have now. </div> </div> </div>I put it to you that I do not 'misunderstand you', but that perhaps you misspoke - or perhaps have changed your stance from that post.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you wish to continue to mischaracterize my words on this forum then I won't stop you but I will ask you to politely inquire as to my opinions instead.<br /> <br /> I am sure you will find my opinions to be far less one dimensional than you thought previously. </div> </div> </div>Your words are not being mischaracterized. Either you poorly expressed yourself, or you now attempt to change your stance, because the grounds you laid out for your sympathies are quite clear.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T06:28:32-08:00","id":1041226,"title":"","content":"I do not think that we need to continue this paricular argument between Zennis and loomer. The Technocrats used, and continues to use, religion to further its goals, much like Nazi Germany or Modern China. While not all religious extremism can be laid at the door of the Technocracy, the current round of extremism from Islamic reactionaries in MENA and the response from Christians in Europe and North America is useful to the Technocracy because bigotry and fear makes populations easier to control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T13:13:13-08:00","id":1041433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041226#post1041226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that we need to continue this paricular argument between Zennis and loomer. The Technocrats used, and continues to use, religion to further its goals, much like Nazi Germany or Modern China. While not all religious extremism can be laid at the door of the Technocracy, the current round of extremism from Islamic reactionaries in MENA and the response from Christians in Europe and North America is useful to the Technocracy because bigotry and fear makes populations easier to control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, and the Union is the primal evil.<br /> <br /> The Batini and Taftani also have nothing to do with that (and actually, are playing the game of the techies unwillingly, believing they're achieving actual victories).<br /> <br /> And people don't like the Union only because of the correlation with real world sciences and technology. The Union is FUN. Fun to play. It's also a totally different game from &quot;Mage the Ascension&quot;. It's like playing two different kind of supernaturals using similar rules.<br /> <br /> And another thing: the Union have good things too. A lot of them (to be fair, the OoR were better, in a time were what would be the Traditions and Crafts were assholes).<br /> <br /> And second: the Union IS humanity's last defense. You may not agree with it, but it is true; nobody else cares... Not even the Traditions. Who keep the nightmares away?<br /> <br /> The Union is indeed a fascist organization. They ARE opressive. The thing is: in the WoD, they are a necessity.<br /> <br /> Can you imagine what the world would be if they suddenly vanished?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:00:58-08:00","id":1041466,"title":"","content":"Fascists are never necessary, though they will twist history in a knot to make themselves seem necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:16:26-08:00","id":1041509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041466#post1041466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fascists are never necessary, though they will twist history in a knot to make themselves seem necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be argued that, if the population is so disgruntled that fascism seems necessary to the majority, then perhaps it becomes an inevitability, and thus fascism is necessary just so it may serve as an example of its consequences.<br /> <br /> Note: This is not an attempt to advocate for fascism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-31-2017, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:17:04-08:00","id":1041510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041466#post1041466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fascists are never necessary, though they will twist history in a knot to make themselves seem necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you in real life. In Mage, though the Technocracy does have a point.<br /> <br /> And the thing is, it isn't that the Technocracy hates Freedom. They want to create a world that is Free and Secure and Imaginative at the same time. They also know that's completely impossible... yet. They are hoping that if they can make humanity ascend they will get the perfect society they want. In real life it wouldn't be possible, but they are Mages, they've seen that the world can be more.<br /> <br /> But in the meantime they will usually sacrifice freedom and imagination for security and control, and every time they do they risk blinding themselves to their true goals.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:42:17-08:00","id":1041528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041510#post1041510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with you in real life. In Mage, though the Technocracy does have a point.<br /> <br /> And the thing is, it isn't that the Technocracy hates Freedom. They want to create a world that is Free and Secure and Imaginative at the same time. They also know that's completely impossible... yet. They are hoping that if they can make humanity ascend they will get the perfect society they want. In real life it wouldn't be possible, but they are Mages, they've seen that the world can be more.<br /> <br /> But in the meantime they will usually sacrifice freedom and imagination for security and control, and every time they do they risk blinding themselves to their true goals.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. And each convention has their own take on what constitutes freedom and control.<br /> <br /> The NWO are advocates of socialism, and state that people should be free to do whatever they want as long as they can know about it, and ensure that people don't abuse their freedom. The people have a right to feel safe.<br /> The Syndicate are advocates of neo-liberalism, and state that people should be free to have access to whatever they want. The people have a right to the pursuit of happiness and the avoidance of stress.<br /> The Progenitors are advocates of medical science, in freedom from the worries of the fragility of life. The people have a right to a healthy life, even if they were dealt a bad hand.<br /> Iteration X are advocates of tech being incorporated into every facet of modern living, in the freedom to move beyond their human limitations and achieve what they yearn for. The people have a right to convenience.<br /> The Voice Engineers are advocates of exploration beyond the known for the sake of protection, and that people should be free to live safe in the knowledge that they are the masters of their destiny without worry of the cosmic horrors which lurk in dark corners. The people have a right to not be in constant fear of that which they cannot comprehend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-31-2017, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:50:25-08:00","id":1041532,"title":"","content":"Of course the Technocracy knows that the world can be more, they have spent over a century and a half making sure that the Masses do not know that the world is more than it appears by committing genocide against every supernatural creature they can find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:05:23-08:00","id":1041544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041532#post1041532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course the Technocracy knows that the world can be more, they have spent over a century and a half making sure that the Masses do not know that the world is more than it appears by committing genocide against every supernatural creature they can find.</div> </div> </div> </div>And their response would probably be: &quot;it's not genocide if it ain't human.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:05:39-08:00","id":1041545,"title":"","content":"Different meaning of the term more.<br /> <br /> Look, I prefer the Traditions, but both sides are a mix of morally admirable and morally blameworthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:28:48-08:00","id":1041560,"title":"","content":"Alright, I will bite, what have the Traditions done in the last century and a half that is comparable to the mundane and supernatural genocides allowed or sponsored by the Technocracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:50:06-08:00","id":1041569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041560#post1041560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I will bite, what have the Traditions done in the last century and a half that is comparable to the mundane and supernatural genocides allowed or sponsored by the Technocracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure if you asked a Garou that, they could talk at length on the number of spirits Tradition mages have enslaved or executed. Especially the Order of Hermes and the Celestial Chorus.<br /> Though even the Dreamspeakers are guilty of this at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T17:22:43-08:00","id":1041578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041560#post1041560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I will bite, what have the Traditions done in the last century and a half that is comparable to the mundane and supernatural genocides allowed or sponsored by the Technocracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe the intent was to say 'one is bad, the other is equally bad', but rather 'both contain good and bad elements and have done good and terrible things.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T17:29:39-08:00","id":1041583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041560#post1041560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I will bite, what have the Traditions done in the last century and a half that is comparable to the mundane and supernatural genocides allowed or sponsored by the Technocracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Allowed? Not participated in, merely stood back and let happen? I am going to have remember that. It's a great example of how to judge the Technocracy by the Traditions values. Usually it is the other way around. You know, things like quality of life metrics when quality of life is a Technocratic way of looking at the world. I like it.<br /> <br /> That said, how many of those supernatural threats were running roughshod over humanity. How many souls were taken? How many babies eaten? How many cut down by something that just wanted a plaything? When humanity has spent most of its existence at the mercy of everything else, its nice to see someone actively looking out for them, for no other reason than that they are human. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T18:41:00-08:00","id":1041623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there#post1039215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, I think that they have misogynistic and racist tendencies because the majority of the members of the Technocracy seem to be European men (with the occasional Asian man from the Five Metal Dragons when they need something from their Asian friends).</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, I realize this was said a while back. But I never really addressed this. It's explicitly stated that wherever the Union operates, the agents used in that place are chosen to look 'nondescript' for that location. When a woman would look most average or normal for the given location, a woman is chosen. When someone of a particular ethnicity would be the least obtrusive, someone of that ethnicity is chosen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T16:21:22-08:00","id":1042105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041510#post1041510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with you in real life. In Mage, though the Technocracy does have a point.<br /> <br /> And the thing is, it isn't that the Technocracy hates Freedom. They want to create a world that is Free and Secure and Imaginative at the same time. They also know that's completely impossible... yet. They are hoping that if they can make humanity ascend they will get the perfect society they want. In real life it wouldn't be possible, but they are Mages, they've seen that the world can be more.<br /> <br /> But in the meantime they will usually sacrifice freedom and imagination for security and control, and every time they do they risk blinding themselves to their true goals.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It indeed has a point. That makes it interesting in my eyes, as a villain. It has a point, but, IMO, that led them to, as I said before to a conclusion that allows them to do things I just can't stand behind.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the problem with war mentality, is that it never ends. There would always be more enemies, more danger that legitimize those horrible acts. After a point it's not the real danger that matters, but simply the using the notion of danger as legitimization for control and do basically what they want.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;humanity's last defense angle&quot;. I don't think so. I don't think that without the Union, humanity would go to hell. The other factions don't want that, because it's bad to business. Moreover, the world went on fine before the Union. Naturally that last part depends on how much you want to exaggerate the shittyness of the Dark Ages and before that in comparison to the real world.<br /> <br /> That they are at least human is an interesting part. For me, if a secret organization makes decisions over my head and without my consent and chance to influence it about basically every part of my life and the whole World, well, in my eyes it's basically irrelevant that they're Technocrats or vampires or whatnot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T16:55:09-08:00","id":1042116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041045#post1041045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear Journal.<br /> <br /> We're 12 pages in and there's no sign of a cease fire.<br /> <br /> Diplomacy has failed, Communications are tense, and appeals of &quot;Guys! You're both right!&quot; have fallen to these steadfast legions.<br /> <br /> On one side, the Anti-crats. Adamant in their assertions that Tech is only a solution for the destruction tech has brought upon the earth.<br /> While opposing them, are the Techno-pros, Unwilling to shift their claim that without Tech there would be no progress, and only stagnation.<br /> <br /> It's hard to think back, all those....4 days ago, how did this all begin? A simple comment, an expression of an opinion. an exchange of conflicting views... Then came the Anthropologists and the Historians, experts in their fields, willing to use real world claims to back up their notes. Then the Canon's were brought out, each one firing an impressive display of completely made up but generally accepted an adhered to facts. The carnage was brutal on all sides was brutal.<br /> Throughout the flurry of History lessons and Source book references, a number of voices were heard, appeals to emotion. Cries for the glory that is tech, anger towards the evil that is control. All of which built up a great catalogue of interpretive thoughts.<br /> <br /> We are all experts. We are all essayists. We are all the masters of our own downfall. Don't you see? We brought this upon ourselves. For each one feels entitled to their own interpretation, but to justify their own convictions, they must destroy any attempt to undermine our own theories. Our own theories about a world which we created, and we have the power to change because it doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> The facts are not facts. The History is optional. The main events are modular. And the masterminds are whatever makes sense at the time. Such ideas cannot be tolerated by either side. There is only one way to interpret this game, only one! Perhaps the only thing either end may agree on is that only one view can stand...<br /> <br /> We are trapped in a bitter war that has no end, no real purpose. As discussion continues to deteriorate, the massive walls of impenetrable explanation are being built, and cries of &quot;Do what you're like, but this is why you're wrong&quot; echo in all directions.<br /> <br /> What is there left to blame? Will an agreement ever be met? If neither side will back down I can only see one logical endpoint.<br /> <br /> Calling each other stupid.<br /> <br /> I pray it will not come to this.<br /> <br /> Signed</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd buy you a drink for that if we'd be in the same city! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> To me, it basically two different things:<br /> <br /> 1. Interpretations of the setting.<br /> 2. What the books say.<br /> <br /> The authors always said that nothing in the books is the Holy Script, that you could change everything to your tastes. And I'm full supporting that. That's just a different thing than arguing about the setting-as-written.<br /> <br /> Like, we could argue about that the Cain and the Antes story of Vampire is silly, that it had to be different than the myth. That doesn't change the fact the the game and the game and setting supports at least the existence of a first vampire and the progenitors of the clans and names quite a few and follows what happened to them.<br /> <br /> So, in the official material, some things left deliberately non-clear to allow for different interpretations even within the official setting. However, the material supports some ideas more than others.<br /> <br /> In the end, it's not about which is &quot;right&quot;. All interpretations are right. It's about what the official setting says.<br /> <br /> To me, the Reality Zones and Earthly Foundations version is more plausible, because I think it's more supported in the books and it's in-line with other gamelines. I just feel, that if you want the Fully Malleable Reality version, you must cut out and change and explain things as falsely created history in a quantity, that it ceases to be the official Mage, and, with a wider scope WoD setting. Every historical record, every other gameline, even Mage's DA version and even more.<br /> <br /> To following up Ramnesis' request (if I'm remembering correctly) to speak about the whys of our choices as preferred interpretations go: aside from the above, because it's basically applying Occam's razor to the question. Moreover, I think that's the version that enables the most diverse games (in the sense of crossover) as it is the most compatible version with other games. Also, it allows for different magical thought schools to coexist without the need of constantly blowing each other up. Also-also, it's just makes the setting more plausible to me, more believable and I'm not THAT humanist, so I like the idea of having a World that's not just about humanity, because I think it's enough of a problem IRL that humans think everything is because of and for the sake of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> At the end, I just want to add that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12880\" data-vbnamecard=\"12880\">Karlgust</a> said somewhere there or on the other topic, that he likes these arguments. For once, I could stand behind THAT. Actually, these discussions, with all their heat, helps me to, for example, getting into the technocratic mindset which helps to portray them in games in a more nuanced way. So, thanks everyone, it's always a pleasure! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 02-01-2017, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T17:41:19-08:00","id":1042135,"title":"","content":"I realized I never put my personal stance on the table openly, so here it is. I'm actually a dirty rotten traditions sympathizer my own self, though as a concept, a storytelling tool, and a setting element I also genuinely like the Technocracy for the sheer amount of versatility and range it offers (and for that matter, my fondness for the Void Engineers goes above and beyond into outright 'they dope as hell' territory.) I can't really be anything but, as a follower of the Thrice-Great, a practicing high-and-low sorcerer, and a man who regularly has dream-conversations with his totem and offers it sacrifice on the regular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T19:09:50-08:00","id":1042170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1042105#post1042105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the &quot;humanity's last defense angle&quot;. I don't think so. I don't think that without the Union, humanity would go to hell. The other factions don't want that, because it's bad to business. Moreover, the world went on fine before the Union. Naturally that last part depends on how much you want to exaggerate the shittyness of the Dark Ages and before that in comparison to the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>You had vampires using humans as toys, insanely powerful Fae stealing babies and cursing entire villages for not doing some crazy oath made by your ancestors 300 years before, werewolves ripping people's spines off for crossing the wrong woods, beast spawned from the pits devouring villagers. Oh, and lets not forget all those Mages living on their Ivory Towers not giving a damn about the ignorant rabble, unworth of their corporal fluids (so, many Mages would suck a human dry just to make experiences with their body fluids).<br /> <br /> Yep, sure, humanity really dont need the Union.<br /> <br /> After all, those Dragons, Krakens, Gorgons, and anything you could find on a D&amp;D Monsters' Book that existed in the world before weren't dangerous at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> [QUOTE=PM\u00e1rk;n1042105That they are at least human is an interesting part. For me, if a secret organization makes decisions over my head and without my consent and chance to influence it about basically every part of my life and the whole World, well, in my eyes it's basically irrelevant that they're Technocrats or vampires or whatnot. [/QUOTE]<br /> Except that the technocrats really DID improve lives of humans. You had Vampire rulers on SEVERAL ocasions - Enoque, Rome, Carthage - look how fine was that and compare.<br /> <br /> Despite every blindness of the Union, they still have noble goals. But others supernaturals do not, so its not the same thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T19:20:04-08:00","id":1042174,"title":"","content":"<i>Parts</i> of the Union have noble goals. Others have long since left those goals behind in favour of the raw accumulation of power, and unfortunately, those parts tend to be fairly influential. It's an important distinction and it underscores every success and failure of the Union.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T19:26:01-08:00","id":1042177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1042174#post1042174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Parts</i> of the Union have noble goals. Others have long since left those goals behind in favour of the raw accumulation of power, and unfortunately, those parts tend to be fairly influential. It's an important distinction and it underscores every success and failure of the Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But still, it isn't the same as if the Sabbat became the &quot;shepperds&quot; of human kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T19:26:21-08:00","id":1042178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1042170#post1042170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You had vampires using humans as toys,</div> </div> </div> </div>And humans using humans as toys all through history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> insanely powerful Fae stealing babies and cursing entire villages for not doing some crazy oath made by your ancestors 300 years before, werewolves ripping people's spines off for crossing the wrong woods, beast spawned from the pits devouring villagers. Oh, and lets not forget all those Mages living on their Ivory Towers not giving a damn about the ignorant rabble, unworth of their corporal fluids (so, many Mages would suck a human dry just to make experiences with their body fluids).<br /> <br /> Yep, sure, humanity really dont need the Union.<br /> <br /> After all, those Dragons, Krakens, Gorgons, and anything you could find on a D&amp;D Monsters' Book that existed in the world before weren't dangerous at all. </div> </div> </div>As I said, the berth of those depends on how much you want to diverge from real-world history and going into grim-dark-fantasy territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except that the technocrats really DID improve lives of humans. You had Vampire rulers on SEVERAL ocasions - Enoque, Rome, Carthage - look how fine was that and compare. </div> </div> </div>As above. We know nothing about Enoch. Rome was the center and at the technological, some might argue cultural peak of the world. Carthage was a great and rich empire for a long time. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite every blindness of the Union, they still have noble goals. But others supernaturals do not, so its not the same thing </div> </div> </div>A tyrant is a tyrant. A technocrat, who want to control every aspect of my life, &quot;for my sake&quot; is no better in my eyes than a religious fanatic, or communist, or whatnot who want to do the same. &quot;We know better what's good for you and society than you&quot; is a dangerous thought. One which led humanity down the path of countless millions suffering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T19:35:48-08:00","id":1042182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1041466#post1041466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fascists are never necessary, though they will twist history in a knot to make themselves seem necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true in the real world.<br /> <br /> In the WoD however, it's not like vampires and werewolves and changellings choose by vote the &quot;supernaturals parliament&quot; toghether with Mages to decide the rules of peaceful coexistence with humanity<br /> <br /> About the whole &quot;supernaturals genocide&quot;... Please. Would you like those inhuman monsters roaming in the nights on our world?<br /> <br /> I don't feel bad for those unholy vampires or furious demonic werewolves that they put down","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T19:47:44-08:00","id":1042185,"title":"","content":"In an age of rationality and sanity, vampires are not unholy, and werewolves are not demonic. The Union disavows the existence of divinity and the supernatural, and even 'vampire' and 'werewolf' are contentious terms. Komrade Karlgust, you will recall from your indoctrination session that the vampire is nothing more than the sufferer of a haemotophagic retrovirus, and the werewolf is not demonic but merely a substrain of EDE that inhabits physical flesh and is capable of reproduction inside the anthroposphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T20:04:04-08:00","id":1042192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1042178#post1042178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A tyrant is a tyrant. A technocrat, who want to control every aspect of my life, &amp;quot;for my sake&amp;quot; is no better in my eyes than a religious fanatic, or communist, or whatnot who want to do the same. &amp;quot;We know better what's good for you and society than you&amp;quot; is a dangerous thought. One which led humanity down the path of countless millions suffering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's fair. For our real world, sure, I agree 100%.<br /> <br /> But the WoD is not the real world.<br /> <br /> That's the only thing: we are not saying the Union are the paladins of the creation. It's not that.<br /> <br /> But, it's just that those who favor the Traditions, don't understand that it's more complex than simply &quot;right vs wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> Besides... Why have the Union always been one step ahead in the Ascension War?<br /> <br /> The answer: the Masses.<br /> <br /> The Union always had the unconcious support of the masses. The Traditions, for all their efforts, never TRULY answered the needs of the masses.<br /> <br /> Hey, when the old OoR arose, the Order of Hermes alone could'd take them down.<br /> <br /> But the Hermetics were busy with political pettyness.<br /> <br /> The OoR went for the little guy. They gave those dirty peasants, who were unworth of the attention of the magestrocracy, tools. Protection. Education.<br /> <br /> The masses, by and at large, gladly embraced the new Consensus.<br /> <br /> That surely says something.<br /> <br /> About the Union being fascist: that's a reflex of people who thinks they are better than the others. That, in fact, seems to be a flaw that all awakened society have, it's not exclusive to the techies.<br /> <br /> And why? Simple... Paradigm. When you have a worldview, which you think it is THE ONLY TRUTH, or at least &quot;the best truth&quot;, it's hard to consider any other view just as valid as yours. All the traditions think they are the coolest guys ever. And not only that: they think the sleepers are misguided, blinded fools. That's the truth: the traditions as a whole, hold the sleepers with contempt. <br /> <br /> Do you doubt? Well, just consider how the Traditions call the mundane humans as &quot;sleepers&quot;, and themselves as &quot;awaken&quot;. Sort of like &quot;those fools follow the technocrat's Paradigm because they are blinded to the thruths that only WE know&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mages are elitists by nature. Why would a Hermetic, or Chorist, or Etherite, or any other, ask the opinion of a dumb sleeper? What the hell do they know?<br /> <br /> That's why the Union thinks they have the right to be humanity's &quot;sheppards&quot;. Because, like all enlightened/awakened, they &quot;know better&quot;.<br /> <br /> Every mage knows whats better for the inferior sleepers, better than the sleepers do, after all, what those deluded apes know right? And this is the root of all the opression of the magestrocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T20:07:51-08:00","id":1042194,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I doubt I would be worried about the creatures that go bump in the night because they are rare. I worry about the mortal neighbors who greet me with a smile every morning because history has shown that those people are capable of handing you over to the fascists (whether they call themselves capatalists, communists, idealists, patriots, or socialists) to buy themselves another night of safety. I fear the cowardly mortals, not the inhuman monsters, because I know where the blow is coming from with the inhuman monsters. I fear the patriotic mortals, not the inhuman monsters, because I may hesitate to defend myself with lethal force against another human, even if they mean to kill me, while I will not hesitate to defend myself with lethal force against an inhuman monster. I fear humans much more than I fear monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T20:10:26-08:00","id":1042196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1042185#post1042185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In an age of rationality and sanity, vampires are not unholy, and werewolves are not demonic. The Union disavows the existence of divinity and the supernatural, and even 'vampire' and 'werewolf' are contentious terms. Komrade Karlgust, you will recall from your indoctrination session that the vampire is nothing more than the sufferer of a haemotophagic retrovirus, and the werewolf is not demonic but merely a substrain of EDE that inhabits physical flesh and is capable of reproduction inside the anthroposphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please komrade loomer, my supervisor doesn't need to know that I know you understand... I'm sure you can be discret with a proper... Incentive. I just need to know what I need to do for you my esteemed friend, in order for you to understand why not report","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T20:16:30-08:00","id":1042200,"title":"","content":"The critters that go bump in the night are not so scarce as to be particularly comforting, at least if we roll with a view of Mage that contains within it the other lines while embracing Mage's story concerns first. Do that and the ratios can drop frighteningly low. Take the Bay Area - it's ratios drop as low as 1:10,000 between the splats in some locations. If I told you that 1 in 10,000 of your neighbours might be a bloodthirsty vampire, a werewolf who won't think twice about gutting you if he thinks you work for the Wyrm, or a demon who would like to enslave you, would you not worry?<br /> <br /> How about 1 in 130?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T20:22:16-08:00","id":1042205,"title":"","content":"1:10,000 is not scary. A silver knife on one boot, a cold iron knife in the other boot, and a couple of stakes in my sleeves. I was better armed going clubbing in some of the more dangerous areas of San Diego when I was in the Navy. I am still more worried about humans at 1:10,000.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T20:28:41-08:00","id":1042208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1042205#post1042205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1:10,000 is not scary. A silver knife on one boot, a cold iron knife in the other boot, and a couple of stakes in my sleeves. I was better armed going clubbing in some of the more dangerous areas of San Diego when I was in the Navy. I am still more worried about humans at 1:10,000.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about 1:130, then? Also, are you seriously suggesting that when you start carrying a wide array of weapons <i>to nightclubs</i> you aren't 'scared'? That's not a sane and rational behaviour anywhere but an active conflict zone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T20:51:14-08:00","id":1042213,"title":"","content":"Who said I wasn't scared? I was scared of the humans who frequented the clubs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T21:24:03-08:00","id":1042223,"title":"","content":"I was born in '80 and spent my formative years hearing and reading about the Jim Joneses, Charles Mansons, Marshall Applewhites, David Koreshes, and Timothy McVeighs of the world. And every time I read...<i>more spirited</i>...attacks on the Technocracy masquerading as would-be defenses of the Traditions, I can't help but think of what McVeigh actually had to say about why he bombed the Murrah building.<br /> <br /> The personal ideologies that spur people to prefer the Traditions to the Technocracy have their dark sides, too. Realize that, and you'll have your answer why people <i>just might</i> like the Technocracy, or even prefer them to the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 02-02-2017, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T22:24:06-08:00","id":1042233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1042223#post1042223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was born in '80 and spent my formative years hearing and reading about the Jim Joneses, Charles Mansons, Marshall Applewhites, David Koreshes, and Timothy McVeighs of the world. And every time I read...<i>more spirited</i>...attacks on the Technocracy masquerading as would-be defenses of the Traditions, I can't help but think of what McVeigh actually had to say about why he bombed the Murrah building.<br /> <br /> The personal ideologies that spur people to prefer the Traditions to the Technocracy have their dark sides, too. Realize that, and you'll have your answer why people <i>just might</i> like the Technocracy, or even prefer them to the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, not only can you have your own cult in Mage, the game has a Background for it. Granted the benefits plateau after you have over 30 followers, so there's less (mechanical) incentive to have hundreds of cultists, and even less incentive to orchestrate a mass suicide. Dead cultists don't support your Paradigm with their belief, after all.<br /> <br /> But then again, Mages aren't immune to making bad mistakes. Or to becoming so high on their hubris that they won't make grand, Jim Jones-esque gestures of madness. I suspect the Traditions have cabals devoted to investigating the Cults within their sect, to make sure they haven't gone off the deep end. Alternative and fringe belief systems have enough bad press, without the genuine articles contributing to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T06:11:39-08:00","id":1042368,"title":"","content":"Less mechanical benefits sure, but if we are using Reality Zone rules a cult of thousands is a reasonable way to go about creating one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T06:25:32-08:00","id":1042376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1042368#post1042368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less mechanical benefits sure, but if we are using Reality Zone rules a cult of thousands is a reasonable way to go about creating one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, if you anticipate death as inevitable, and you know what happens to Wraiths when they first emerge in the deadlands. Organising a mass suicide to ensure an army of followers in the shadowlands could be a viable tactic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T07:46:40-08:00","id":1042411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite every blindness of the Union, they still have noble goals. But others supernaturals do not, so its not the same thing. </div> </div> </div>Depends on the supernatural. The Union is a faction of Mages. There are factions of Werewolves who have noble goals. They just don't necessarily align with what is best for humanity. Because what is best for humanity is not necessarily of benefit to the world.<br /> Arguably some Vampire factions do as well. The Inconnu.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T07:55:26-08:00","id":1042414,"title":"","content":"Well, the Garou goals are best for humanity as a species because the species will go extinct if the Wyrm wins. It should also be noted that Garou do not go out of their way to kill humans (that is the job of the Ratkin), they tend to go after corporations that hire humans, the equipment that humans use to destroy the environment, the Fomori co-workers that humans work with, etc. If you are illegally dumping radioactive or toxic sludge in the local wilderness of in the local water supply though, they will kill first and ask question later, but you deserve it for poisoning the environment and your fellow man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T08:55:01-08:00","id":1042452,"title":"","content":"Order of Hermes/Cultist of ectasy / virtual adept in here !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T10:40:14-08:00","id":1043630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1042411#post1042411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the supernatural. The Union is a faction of Mages. There are factions of Werewolves who have noble goals. They just don't necessarily align with what is best for humanity. Because what is best for humanity is not necessarily of benefit to the world.<br /> Arguably some Vampire factions do as well. The Inconnu.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as I'm human, I'll think about what's best for humanity... And the unnatural beasts may be damned","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T10:55:06-08:00","id":1043638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1043630#post1043630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As long as I'm human, I'll think about what's best for humanity... And the unnatural beasts may be damned</div> </div> </div> </div>Or rather what you/the Union/any other faction thinks is best for humanity, quite a big difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T11:00:03-08:00","id":1043640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039215-are-there-any-tradition-mages-out-there?p=1043638#post1043638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or rather what you/the Union/any other faction thinks is best for humanity, quite a big difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>The masses don't think, they are sheep, nothing more. We, the Union, will give them what's best for 'em, even when they don't want it, because the masses are like children, don't know what they truly wants or why. But the enlightened do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T11:18:37-08:00","id":1043646,"title":"","content":"Just like any other form of autocracy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T13:06:12-08:00","id":1043696,"title":"","content":"I never played a Technocrat (besides as NPC).<br /> <br /> Technomancers, sure. Magic+Tech was especially appalling for me.<br /> Technoshaman, Dreamwalker, Mr. Vulgar and friends.<br /> <br /> Announcement: My vote can be bought for the measly price of a signature on this totally harmless but sophisticated contract. ;-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So